.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[FIX] [Security] Replace prototype-pollution guards with Map-based storage (#3751)\n\n## 📝 Description\nFixes 7 CodeQL `js/remote-property-injection` alerts (advanced query suite). Replaces per-site `__proto__` guards with `Map`-based storage, which removes the prototype-chain risk at the root. `js/indirect-command-line-injection` in `scripts/testui.js` is intentionally left out of scope.\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Changes Made\n- `secretKeys`, `iguazioProjectsRelations`, `iguazioUserRelations` (`mock.js`) → `Map`; all call sites updated\n- Removed the now-redundant `isUnsafeObjectKey`/`rejectIfUnsafeKey`/`safeAssign` guards from `security.js`\n- `getNuclioShardLags` (`mock.js`) and `fetchMissingProjectPermission` (`workflow.util.js`) build objects via `Object.fromEntries([[key, value]])` instead of computed property names\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Checklist\n\n- [x] I have given the PR a well-structured title describing the domain and the specific change that was made\n- [x] I confirmed that existing tests pass\n- [x] I checked that this change doesn’t introduce new console warnings or lint / formatting errors\n\n---\n\n## 🚨 Potentially Breaking Changes\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No","tree":{"sha":"db16e2c5f70fa57c2fdc9463242b78cebd13f596","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/trees/db16e2c5f70fa57c2fdc9463242b78cebd13f596"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/commits/ca341687df8ea73f5ba8c308541c376b65323a41","verification":{"payload":"tree db16e2c5f70fa57c2fdc9463242b78cebd13f596\nparent 774b82e7b02deba539a3431e3322f11af89c236b\nauthor arturrybalskyy-dev <artur.rybalskyy@globallogic.com> 1787059965 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787059965 +0300\n\n[FIX] [Security] Replace prototype-pollution guards with Map-based storage (#3751)\n\n## 📝 Description\nFixes 7 CodeQL `js/remote-property-injection` alerts (advanced query suite). Replaces per-site `__proto__` guards with `Map`-based storage, which removes the prototype-chain risk at the root. `js/indirect-command-line-injection` in `scripts/testui.js` is intentionally left out of scope.\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Changes Made\n- `secretKeys`, `iguazioProjectsRelations`, `iguazioUserRelations` (`mock.js`) → `Map`; all call sites updated\n- Removed the now-redundant `isUnsafeObjectKey`/`rejectIfUnsafeKey`/`safeAssign` guards from `security.js`\n- `getNuclioShardLags` (`mock.js`) and `fetchMissingProjectPermission` (`workflow.util.js`) build objects via `Object.fromEntries([[key, value]])` instead of computed property names\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Checklist\n\n- [x] I have given the PR a well-structured title describing the domain and the specific change that was made\n- [x] I confirmed that existing tests pass\n- [x] I checked that this change doesn’t introduce new console warnings or lint / formatting errors\n\n---\n\n## 🚨 Potentially Breaking Changes\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhF79CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjG8QAAVAbiVzZFNQQ692TN5ELox9\n+0Cz81120IxTL/+kan4GRfA/wxcg/iC9YimUwjE3d+m0N/R1ELSDceK9tvGPX8rH\nM259Qt6cDod4c5IidDxNx/GLPR7TOYfJehRggPDVHvh4/KvI+en+o8uSP9i1EYrR\nZL9wkSimpnJpow/pk+d/Cp500WJlT9z2A8oypTJ4chzCy7loryu5zyWoV4O0Qrga\nCFTNFp0xHr+CLaxkcdJs9Zpt8KZ5Nqk2r03o0Je9wFwhzm7opGpr5RkM7h2gZx7l\nJCeyZtMIScF6YvShEWcVwOupxk+ytDz3mfjVKVqaN+NupTgqvzA3pR3tsKiC8GCY\nxjdw7Pdp21zJ8/CF/SFtiqivAl78B0CfcS6ApqZ1nvdwVxtbC7W+5+JbDlakqfla\nE5sz5GAZVJIpFiQLo4moPo2K7HfVCu5HgaSk3pOEhhl/mCQSIR+UF3rHCcMlktWn\nDObmCutNt894ZOYUTXaEw0PopgbwBaRONT0sLQoTHRwZwYG4BqFXD9oZUF20Wd8S\nyqCBXRHC18l4ne4F0VRZrYtwObLS83Ix7fFWz7jgtkkPM5OE3ZyYJ3Ns2o8ZHX6Y\n7IHF6buqkkWY6y0t/J4GIfTxf5RP+eUP+Zfug9i/U5bo2Dk15x+rwrwKEONCR0Up\neqpRP6uJr/79O34a+zQW\n=SDA5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T13:32:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mlrun/ui/commit/ca341687df8ea73f5ba8c308541c376b65323a41","node_id":"C_kwDODbfsqtoAKGNhMzQxNjg3ZGY4ZWE3M2Y1YmE4YzMwODU0MWMzNzZiNjUzMjNhNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mlrun/ui/commit/774b82e7b02deba539a3431e3322f11af89c236b","sha":"774b82e7b02deba539a3431e3322f11af89c236b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/774b82e7b02deba539a3431e3322f11af89c236b"}],"sha":"ca341687df8ea73f5ba8c308541c376b65323a41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/ca341687df8ea73f5ba8c308541c376b65323a41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249736548?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arturrybalskyy-dev","id":249736548,"login":"arturrybalskyy-dev","node_id":"U_kgDODuKtZA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arturrybalskyy-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/774b82e7b02deba539a3431e3322f11af89c236b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T10:33:58Z","email":"artur.rybalskyy@globallogic.com","name":"arturrybalskyy-dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T10:33:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[FIX] [Tests] Resolve CodeQL code scanning alerts in mock server (#3749)\n\n[FIX] [Tests] Resolve CodeQL code scanning alerts in mock server\n\n## 📝 Description\nCloses all 51 GitHub Code Scanning (CodeQL) alerts on the mock server, spanning reflected-xss, type-confusion-through-parameter-tampering, path-injection, prototype-polluting-assignment, loop-bound-injection, missing-rate-limiting, insecure-randomness, and incomplete-sanitization\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Changes Made\n- xss: `res.send(obj)` → `res.json(obj)` for JSON payloads; explicit `text/plain` for the one real string response\n- type-confusion: `typeof`/`Array.isArray` guards on `req.query`/`req.params` before string methods (native `Array.isArray`, not lodash''s, which CodeQL doesn''t treat as a barrier)\n- path-injection: inline `indexOf(''..'')` + resolved-path containment check at `getFile`/`getFileStats` (also caught an unguarded arbitrary file read in `getFile` that wasn''t part of the original alert set); `resolveFunctionYAMLPath()` for the function-template routes\n- prototype-pollution: inline `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` key checks at each sink (`secretKeys`, `iguazioProjectsRelations`)\n- loop-bound-injection: `boundArray()` applied at each iteration site (`chunk`/`orderBy`/`forEach`), rejecting non-arrays\n- rate-limiting: `express-rate-limit` (new devDependency) applied to all 10 routes that actually touch the filesystem\n- insecure-randomness: `Math.random()` → `crypto.randomInt()` in `makeUID()` and the prompt-pool picker\n- incomplete-sanitization: escape backslashes before dots in `getRule()`\n- new `tests/mockServer/security.js` holds the reusable hardening helpers instead of inlining them all in `mock.js`\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Checklist\n\n- [x] I have given the PR a well-structured title describing the domain and the specific change that was made\n- [x] I confirmed that existing tests pass\n- [x] I checked that this change doesn’t introduce new console warnings or lint / formatting errors\n\n---\n\n## 🚨 Potentially Breaking Changes\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No","tree":{"sha":"3ed6bbee818871255cfac890e6679c7c8f3ebbc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/trees/3ed6bbee818871255cfac890e6679c7c8f3ebbc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/commits/774b82e7b02deba539a3431e3322f11af89c236b","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ed6bbee818871255cfac890e6679c7c8f3ebbc6\nparent 87f84d91c29aaa0966d9ec7b35ca9721a2374d0c\nauthor arturrybalskyy-dev <artur.rybalskyy@globallogic.com> 1787049238 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787049238 +0300\n\n[FIX] [Tests] Resolve CodeQL code scanning alerts in mock server (#3749)\n\n[FIX] [Tests] Resolve CodeQL code scanning alerts in mock server\n\n## 📝 Description\nCloses all 51 GitHub Code Scanning (CodeQL) alerts on the mock server, spanning reflected-xss, type-confusion-through-parameter-tampering, path-injection, prototype-polluting-assignment, loop-bound-injection, missing-rate-limiting, insecure-randomness, and incomplete-sanitization\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Changes Made\n- xss: `res.send(obj)` → `res.json(obj)` for JSON payloads; explicit `text/plain` for the one real string response\n- type-confusion: `typeof`/`Array.isArray` guards on `req.query`/`req.params` before string methods (native `Array.isArray`, not lodash''s, which CodeQL doesn''t treat as a barrier)\n- path-injection: inline `indexOf(''..'')` + resolved-path containment check at `getFile`/`getFileStats` (also caught an unguarded arbitrary file read in `getFile` that wasn''t part of the original alert set); `resolveFunctionYAMLPath()` for the function-template routes\n- prototype-pollution: inline `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` key checks at each sink (`secretKeys`, `iguazioProjectsRelations`)\n- loop-bound-injection: `boundArray()` applied at each iteration site (`chunk`/`orderBy`/`forEach`), rejecting non-arrays\n- rate-limiting: `express-rate-limit` (new devDependency) applied to all 10 routes that actually touch the filesystem\n- insecure-randomness: `Math.random()` → `crypto.randomInt()` in `makeUID()` and the prompt-pool picker\n- incomplete-sanitization: escape backslashes before dots in `getRule()`\n- new `tests/mockServer/security.js` holds the reusable hardening helpers instead of inlining them all in `mock.js`\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Checklist\n\n- [x] I have given the PR a well-structured title describing the domain and the specific change that was made\n- [x] I confirmed that existing tests pass\n- [x] I checked that this change doesn’t introduce new console warnings or lint / formatting errors\n\n---\n\n## 🚨 Potentially Breaking Changes\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhDUWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoCIQAEZpz0kE1ZOuRdRf3ZswJ8Dv\n2ZQ/9pmIuftQ8iikJ8drg3yDoHIA3GIHv+wDvbq+y7uM/IwJdN/s5ZYL8m2hsczg\nz/U/xu6zTIysrrNZGQXNEoMBal22rOlIjwqnPAom+hXYw8J0AORtQzX/S9vdyfFv\nbp7FN2nTbkZmN1BanAWe8WbRQrDew9gs+QvvEhiv/wppo1j5wuhkUkTL5mthLWzx\nOHZbyC1IkCz/+5hpMSUG0D3kA1Dskd/GIfrrj5+H5ykWhVj3GssiycxuEPohc3S8\nTv00dlRdsEX28UhAyE/TmaLaZAsd4KmaEZ60TWdUYrb4csYqHxFVguOsNojephUO\nLTC4PAjtUU/UOpEuZtgbwPGafd9U5S/ImM/GFnrWmyQnbMJ0N+Ks6rV1WnK1miw2\n+zPw9SXx9Tul3aNJ5xNSSUCipINaJVrR2Dh3vbWa3mGlLRwQCdY75T2zS+o4ZhTx\nTeRkF9eBIhLKZc4Vd2YmzijIvJ+YE2D++GmCHYJlQTlGHhxYXtQ3