"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mlrun/ui/commit/3f700b69c55eac5303a6152ecef65197d4d0d302","node_id":"C_kwDODbfsqtoAKDNmNzAwYjY5YzU1ZWFjNTMwM2E2MTUyZWNlZjY1MTk3ZDRkMGQzMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mlrun/ui/commit/e84b0adcd7a31c8e04aeea5b5dc27cc620cae9cc","sha":"e84b0adcd7a31c8e04aeea5b5dc27cc620cae9cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/e84b0adcd7a31c8e04aeea5b5dc27cc620cae9cc"}],"sha":"3f700b69c55eac5303a6152ecef65197d4d0d302","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/3f700b69c55eac5303a6152ecef65197d4d0d302"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63646693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ilan7empest","id":63646693,"login":"ilan7empest","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNjQ2Njkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilan7empest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/e84b0adcd7a31c8e04aeea5b5dc27cc620cae9cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T08:29:56Z","email":"63646693+ilan7empest@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ilank"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T08:29:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[FIX] uuid: Missing buffer bounds check in v3/v5/v6 when buf is provided\n\n<!-- Title structure should start with a flag - either of these:\n  [FEAT] [FIX] [CHORE] [CI] [DOCS] [STYLE] [REFACTOR] [TEST] [BUILD] [PERF]\nFollowed by a clear representation - e.g:\n  [STYLE] Reformat components for linting compliance\n  [CI] Run tests on push for all branches\n  [FEAT] Add dark mode toggle in header\n  -->\n  \n  ## 📝 Description\n  <!-- A clear, concise summary of what this PR does. -->\n  <!-- Include context, motivation, or related issues (e.g., \"Replaces Sass with CSS Modules\"). -->\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Changes Made\n  <!-- List the main updates in this PR. -->\n<!-- Example:\n  - Replaced Sass styles with CSS Modules\n  - Updated Button component props for accessibility\n  - Adjusted CI workflow to run on push for all branches\n  -->\n\n**Situation**\nThe app already depended on uuid@^14.0.0, which includes the [GHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq) fix (buffer bounds for v3/v5/v6).\nTransitive copies were still older: Storybook on 9.x, Cucumber on 11.x, and cucumber-html-reporter on the legacy 3.x line.\n\n**Change**\n1. overrides.uuid: \"^14.0.0\" so every consumer of the modern uuid package resolves to ≥ 14.0.0 (aligned with the patched release).\n\n2. overrides.cucumber-html-reporter.uuid: \"^3.4.0\" so that package keeps npm uuid@3.x. A flat override to 14 breaks it: it loads uuid/v4, which is not in the exports of uuid@14 (ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED). That old major is a different implementation than the one in the advisory (src/v35.ts / v6.ts on the current package).\n\n**Checks**\n- npm ls uuid: app + Storybook + Cucumber → 14.0.0; cucumber-html-reporter → 3.4.0 nested.\n- require(''cucumber-html-reporter'') succeeds.\n- On 14.0.0, v4 / v5 / v6 with an 8-byte buffer and offset 4 all throw RangeError (matches the intended fix).\n\n```\npackage.json\nLines 58-62\n  \"overrides\": {\n    \"uuid\": \"^14.0.0\",\n    \"cucumber-html-reporter\": {\n      \"uuid\": \"^3.4.0\"\n    },\n```\nNote: scanners may still report uuid@3.4.0 under cucumber-html-reporter. If you need a clean audit there too, the durable approach is to move off cucumber-html-reporter or use a fork/release that depends on modern uuid and updated imports.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have given the PR a well-structured title describing the domain and the specific change that was made\n- [x] I tested the changes in the browser (locally or via preview build)\n- [x] I confirmed that existing tests pass\n- [ ] I added or updated unit / integration tests (if needed)\n- [ ] I checked that this change doesn’t introduce new console warnings or lint / formatting errors\n- [ ] I updated the relevant Jira ticket with the appropriate details and status\n\n\n---\n\n## 🔗 References\n- Related ticket / issue: [ML-12483](https://iguazio.atlassian.net/browse/ML-12483)\n- Figma / design spec:\n- Documentation:\n\n---\n\n## 🚨 Potentially Breaking Changes\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No\n\n<!-- If yes, describe what breaks and how to migrate: -->\n<!-- Example: Renamed prop `variant` → `type` in Button component -->\n\n---\n\nIncludes DRC change\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No\n\nIf yes -> requires bump NPM version\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Additional Notes\n<!-- Optional: other context, performance considerations, or follow-up work -->\n<!-- Example:\n  - TODO: Migrate remaining components away from Sass\n  - Known issue: minor layout flicker on mobile\n  -->\n\n---\n\n## 📸 Screenshots / Demos\n<!-- Include before/after screenshots, GIFs, or video demos if the change affects UI. -->\n<!-- You can drag and drop images here directly in the PR. -->\n\n---\n\n\n[ML-12483]: https://iguazio.atlassian.net/browse/ML-12483?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","tree":{"sha":"4521cd3dd35fe4d4d37604d66097c81c9d393622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/trees/4521cd3dd35fe4d4d37604d66097c81c9d393622"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/commits/e84b0adcd7a31c8e04aeea5b5dc27cc620cae9cc","verification":{"payload":"tree 4521cd3dd35fe4d4d37604d66097c81c9d393622\nparent 5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59\nauthor Ilank <63646693+ilan7empest@users.noreply.github.com> 1778574596 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778574596 +0300\n\n[FIX] uuid: Missing buffer bounds check in v3/v5/v6 when buf is provided\n\n<!-- Title structure should start with a flag - either of these:\n  [FEAT] [FIX] [CHORE] [CI] [DOCS] [STYLE] [REFACTOR] [TEST] [BUILD] [PERF]\nFollowed by a clear representation - e.g:\n  [STYLE] Reformat components for linting compliance\n  [CI] Run tests on push for all branches\n  [FEAT] Add dark mode toggle in header\n  -->\n  \n  ## 📝 Description\n  <!-- A clear, concise summary of what this PR does. -->\n  <!-- Include context, motivation, or related issues (e.g., \"Replaces Sass with CSS Modules\"). -->\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Changes Made\n  <!-- List the main updates in this PR. -->\n<!-- Example:\n  - Replaced Sass styles with CSS Modules\n  - Updated Button component props for accessibility\n  - Adjusted CI workflow to run on push for all branches\n  -->\n\n**Situation**\nThe app already depended on uuid@^14.0.0, which includes the [GHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq) fix (buffer bounds for v3/v5/v6).\nTransitive copies were still older: Storybook on 9.x, Cucumber on 11.x, and cucumber-html-reporter on the legacy 3.x line.\n\n**Change**\n1. overrides.uuid: \"^14.0.0\" so every consumer of the modern uuid package resolves to ≥ 14.0.0 (aligned with the patched release).\n\n2. overrides.cucumber-html-reporter.uuid: \"^3.4.0\" so that package keeps npm uuid@3.x. A flat override to 14 breaks it: it loads uuid/v4, which is not in the exports of uuid@14 (ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED). That old major is a different implementation than the one in the advisory (src/v35.ts / v6.ts on the current package).\n\n**Checks**\n- npm ls uuid: app + Storybook + Cucumber → 14.0.0; cucumber-html-reporter → 3.4.0 nested.\n- require(''cucumber-html-reporter'') succeeds.\n- On 14.0.0, v4 / v5 / v6 with an 8-byte buffer and offset 4 all throw RangeError (matches the intended fix).\n\n```\npackage.json\nLines 58-62\n  \"overrides\": {\n    \"uuid\": \"^14.0.0\",\n    \"cucumber-html-reporter\": {\n      \"uuid\": \"^3.4.0\"\n    },\n```\nNote: scanners may still report uuid@3.4.0 under cucumber-html-reporter. If you need a clean audit there too, the durable approach is to move off cucumber-html-reporter or use a fork/release that depends on modern uuid and updated imports.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have given the PR a well-structured title describing the domain and the specific change that was made\n- [x] I tested the changes in the browser (locally or via preview build)\n- [x] I confirmed that existing tests pass\n- [ ] I added or updated unit / integration tests (if needed)\n- [ ] I checked that this change doesn’t introduce new console warnings or lint / formatting errors\n- [ ] I updated the relevant Jira ticket with the appropriate details and status\n\n\n---\n\n## 🔗 References\n- Related ticket / issue: [ML-12483](https://iguazio.atlassian.net/browse/ML-12483)\n- Figma / design spec:\n- Documentation:\n\n---\n\n## 🚨 Potentially Breaking Changes\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No\n\n<!-- If yes, describe what breaks and how to migrate: -->\n<!-- Example: Renamed prop `variant` → `type` in Button component -->\n\n---\n\nIncludes DRC change\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No\n\nIf yes -> requires bump NPM version\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Additional Notes\n<!-- Optional: other context, performance considerations, or follow-up work -->\n<!-- Example:\n  - TODO: Migrate remaining components away from Sass\n  - Known issue: minor layout flicker on mobile\n  -->\n\n---\n\n## 📸 Screenshots / Demos\n<!-- Include before/after screenshots, GIFs, or video demos if the change affects UI. -->\n<!-- You can drag and drop images here directly in the PR. -->\n\n---\n\n\n[ML-12483]: https://iguazio.atlassian.net/browse/ML-12483?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAuUECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtU4QAFtUGd0EbwFm6p7SSA+epK5u\nuRVAeFwtAfOQ7rUpgx98HqhL4QpZnm9w/A8hf0wvXiZRtgGSbVzWvKhfsEKt/k2L\nnRcYFSci5d5MAVcy9ONDGQMS/XaPojpfKLVAxrp6cbzINwnvRczjzXmkWdLVIHdC\nLWOWO3Yg0PmJMgV+6EAYL+Hb64C5WC5Pivt4LmEAbHezK69OWgERBF+nbXR+s6Oa\n0r/VEON6LYXY8kmLIWbSDu8FWX3vIpykixLA93y7rbfSBqi2LcaKk48y0W5Taa2i\n8v0Fpoh+ZYqQVBKdyEGgn/FLCyOyNkgxQzousIv2kMbL9p5LYAWKYQLhJRwHRCF/\nvvjBq0iL4Vv1oIUm/17xREPoYH9pU+8gWlZU9CoQQbWX1zkovFY3WG34xPGXbThb\n1mmIb6IM6UXXDPiVx1+7vDFLij4r8t9yxr9253oNRw7gsgkzSGw1xdyl1mrpDwVR\nVOwsztCCi+r6Ie+oZ86DHvW3myx5SkcOp4j6LGKBslMiY2Xg1pewQvDwJ3VSBXJ+\nZBSeQGUKiE+VneUZLKTCwBy6duCnINX4FW8FqYacxad0FTlLmQAcRUebJ1TV1BqL\nsurOyS2jjudodCHDXMF5iIIZEh7hkRwP4pf+/C33qQJbKUmaBAsOe02tGTt6/WfG\nGN68GbGazHDuKcFBfDgO\n=dLy2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T08:29:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mlrun/ui/commit/e84b0adcd7a31c8e04aeea5b5dc27cc620cae9cc","node_id":"C_kwDODbfsqtoAKGU4NGIwYWRjZDdhMzFjOGUwNGFlZWE1YjVkYzI3Y2M2MjBjYWU5Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mlrun/ui/commit/5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59","sha":"5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59"}],"sha":"e84b0adcd7a31c8e04aeea5b5dc27cc620cae9cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/e84b0adcd7a31c8e04aeea5b5dc27cc620cae9cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31961495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/muli-cohen","id":31961495,"login":"muli-cohen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTYxNDk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muli-cohen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T16:39:34Z","email":"31961495+muli-cohen@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Muli Cohen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T16:39:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[FIX] Support IPv6 nameservers in nginx resolver config\n\n  ## 📝 Description\n  In IPv6 Kubernetes clusters, the mlrun-ui pod fails to start with `invalid port in resolver` because nginx requires IPv6 addresses to be wrapped in square brackets. The `awk` command in the Dockerfile `CMD` writes bare IPv6 addresses (e.g. `fd00::10`) into `/etc/nginx/resolvers.conf`, and nginx misinterprets the colons as port separators.\n\n  ---\n  ## 🛠️ Changes Made\n  - Updated the `awk` command in the Dockerfile `CMD` to detect IPv6 nameservers (containing `:`) and wrap them in square brackets (`[address]`)\n  - IPv4 addresses are unaffected — fully backward-compatible\n  ---\n  ## ✅ Checklist\n  - [x] I have given the PR a well-structured title describing the domain and the specific change that was made\n  - [x] I tested the changes in the browser (locally or via preview build)\n  - [x] I confirmed that existing tests pass\n  - [x] I checked that this change doesn''t introduce new console warnings or lint / formatting errors\n  - [x] I updated the relevant Jira ticket with the appropriate details and status\n  ---\n  ## 🔗 References\n  - Related ticket / issue:https://ecliptos.atlassian.net/browse/ML-12498\n  - Figma / design spec: N/A\n  - Documentation:\n  ---\n  ## 🚨 Potentially Breaking Changes\n  - [ ] Yes\n  - [x] No\n  ---\n  Includes DRC change\n  - [ ] Yes\n  - [x] No\n  ---\n  ## 🔍 Additional Notes\n  - The fix handles all three scenarios: IPv4-only, IPv6-only, and dual-stack clusters\n  - Example outputs:\n    - IPv4: `resolver 10.96.0.10 ;`\n    - IPv6: `resolver [fd00::10] ;`\n    - Dual-stack: `resolver 10.96.0.10 [fd00::10] ;`\n  ---\n  ## 📸 Screenshots / Demos\n  N/A - no UI changes; infrastructure/config fix only.\n\n  ---","tree":{"sha":"cbceb8bb874e4ac3ffe5a7c3dacf03fc1d4cbec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/trees/cbceb8bb874e4ac3ffe5a7c3dacf03fc1d4cbec3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/commits/5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59","verification":{"payload":"tree cbceb8bb874e4ac3ffe5a7c3dacf03fc1d4cbec3\nparent c0143648b0e997b236f62b8ac603ef849946b4b4\nauthor Muli Cohen <31961495+muli-cohen@users.noreply.github.com> 1778517574 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778517574 +0300\n\n[FIX] Support IPv6 nameservers in nginx resolver config\n\n  ## 📝 Description\n  In IPv6 Kubernetes clusters, the mlrun-ui pod fails to start with `invalid port in resolver` because nginx requires IPv6 addresses to be wrapped in square brackets. The `awk` command in the Dockerfile `CMD` writes bare IPv6 addresses (e.g. `fd00::10`) into `/etc/nginx/resolvers.conf`, and nginx misinterprets the colons as port separators.\n\n  ---\n  ## 🛠️ Changes Made\n  - Updated the `awk` command in the Dockerfile `CMD` to detect IPv6 nameservers (containing `:`) and wrap them in square brackets (`[address]`)\n  - IPv4 addresses are unaffected — fully backward-compatible\n  ---\n  ## ✅ Checklist\n  - [x] I have given the PR a well-structured title describing the domain and the specific change that was made\n  - [x] I tested the changes in the browser (locally or via preview build)\n  - [x] I confirmed that existing tests pass\n  - [x] I checked that this change doesn''t introduce new console warnings or lint / formatting errors\n  - [x] I updated the relevant Jira ticket with the appropriate details and status\n  ---\n  ## 🔗 References\n  - Related ticket / issue:https://ecliptos.atlassian.net/browse/ML-12498\n  - Figma / design spec: N/A\n  - Documentation:\n  ---\n  ## 🚨 Potentially Breaking Changes\n  - [ ] Yes\n  - [x] No\n  ---\n  Includes DRC change\n  - [ ] Yes\n  - [x] No\n  ---\n  ## 🔍 Additional Notes\n  - The fix handles all three scenarios: IPv4-only, IPv6-only, and dual-stack clusters\n  - Example outputs:\n    - IPv4: `resolver 10.96.0.10 ;`\n    - IPv6: `resolver [fd00::10] ;`\n    - Dual-stack: `resolver 10.96.0.10 [fd00::10] ;`\n  ---\n  ## 📸 Screenshots / Demos\n  N/A - no UI changes; infrastructure/config fix only.\n\n  ---","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAgZGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAURIQAHheNSIU51q9EiqEx1obOS77\nA6keGH6YWnq1Uk7iWkagtoyCKzejFto0jLPrII/GGJkCS/lRjOcMiSVg4ZvdZ3PP\nfq8XcXOmuCf3+R9H1aW65Aq3mZVU0aGf3exkBfdcNwJI09kHbOo+N9UexCbY1WEe\nxq18sHhc01xVEzQ75rPsW36RXk2gmBxVhrjfVmSo3+hHQKtBkclMSvhy+sQaMnk1\nMQuFzuyQaoQGzvi+RIVl7wcuZSpSY2hHUodZTy/GTJ5jKVStNfvmsdZTwFZgAMh7\ntf2uqQGDu0swSX5RK0PdRq4eanjr8Q42huSanKayy5kxChOCRZHfoHkABGL8JTHr\nRp6mEc7U+ejgPHWqs/sj4IOO8CzeOkWfB3yAI+yLFulw1cfeI4M1YPWzWsAanGda\nPCh4pHppmzQv8VvhGTT4o4BdOKjfJ0Vr/PvC1oDs+Z/lLILThCpr2KbP4JF84GK7\norEvwPhkircvqFZA4ylSUC2DAVlpkCDedcxqCvCDNgF8w4AoapDWfzDfKmYDO94L\n2AJ382UPBlIvRu5t29Vf+d8oV6axV5FWUMc3OeZF3KmuCdws+r3QFSL6WgVvYzoN\nGLVRqxHzWJVeR/N3kyL0Mosd+UfdJ7jwxCXt6QArfj7Rmc7SFdMhym0XE9EaFxap\nRkJEHMdoB4b+jxHhefCz\n=wczD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T16:39:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mlrun/ui/commit/5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59","node_id":"C_kwDODbfsqtoAKDU3NzZkN2VkZmZlYTM4NTk4NmViYzE5Yjc4YmQyOTQ5MTA3NmVmNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mlrun/ui/commit/c0143648b0e997b236f62b8ac603ef849946b4b4","sha":"c0143648b0e997b236f62b8ac603ef849946b4b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/c0143648b0e997b236f62b8ac603ef849946b4b4"}],"sha":"5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/5776d7edffea385986ebc19b78bd29491076ef59"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38469994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jmcdonagh88","id":38469994,"login":"jmcdonagh88","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NDY5OTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdonagh88","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/commits/c0143648b0e997b236f62b8ac603ef849946b4b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T05:58:15Z","email":"38469994+jmcdonagh88@users.noreply.github.com","name":"James McDonagh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T05:58:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Workflow] Add workflow_call trigger for cross-repo reusable builds (#3660)\n\n* [Workflow] Add workflow_call trigger for cross-repo reusable builds\n\nEnable the UI build workflow to be called directly from mlrun/mlrun\nas a reusable workflow, eliminating the need for token-based polling.\nAdds a ref input for specifying the branch to checkout, and updates\nall input references to use inputs.* for compatibility with both\nworkflow_dispatch and workflow_call triggers.\n\n* fix: remove secrets inherit from workflow_call trigger definition\n\n* fix: always checkout mlrun/ui and simplify job condition\n\nThe github context in reusable workflows reflects the caller''s context,\nso github.event_name is workflow_dispatch (not workflow_call) and\ngithub.repository is the caller''s repo. Hardcode repository to mlrun/ui\nsince this workflow always builds UI code.\n\n* feat: update GitHub Actions workflow to support Artifactory integration\n\n- Made `docker_registries` input optional and added `artifactory_docker_repo` input for specifying Artifactory repository.\n- Updated logic to determine `mlrun_docker_registries` based on the presence of Artifactory inputs.\n- Adjusted Docker login condition to include Artifactory repository input.","tree":{"sha":"269aa01044d009d80eefa1d406da8eb6bc72440d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/trees/269aa01044d009d80eefa1d406da8eb6bc72440d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlrun/ui/git/commits/c0143648b0e997b236f62b8ac603ef849946b4b4","verification":{"payload":"tree 269aa01044d009d80eefa1d406da8eb6bc72440d\nparent 38c8a0245c5476ee2259c8758f5432d518df15c1\nauthor James McDonagh <38469994+jmcdonagh88@users.noreply.github.com> 1777442295 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777442295 +0300\n\n[Workflow] Add workflow_call trigger for cross-repo reusable builds (#3660)\n\n* [Workflow] Add workflow_call trigger for cross-repo reusable builds\n\nEnable the UI build workflow to be called directly from mlrun/mlrun\nas a reusable workflow, eliminating the need for token-based polling.\nAdds a ref input for specifying the branch to checkout, and updates\nall input references to use inputs.* for compatibility with both\nworkflow_dispatch and workflow_call triggers.\n\n* fix: remove secrets inherit from workflow_call trigger definition\n\n* fix: always checkout mlrun/ui and simplify job condition\n\nThe github context in reusable workflows reflects the caller''s context,\nso github.event_name is workflow_dispatch (not workflow_call) and\ngithub.repository is the caller''s repo. Hardcode repository to mlrun/ui\nsince this workflow always builds UI code.\n\n* feat: update GitHub Actions workflow to support Artifactory integration\n\n- Made `docker_registries` input optional and added `artifactory_docker_repo` input for specifying Artifactory repository.\n- Updated logic to determine `mlrun_docker_registries` based on the presence of Artifactory inputs.\n- Adjusted Docker login condition to include Artifactory repository input.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8Z33CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhrgQAH0uCgL8f3mpFccYPZuiERwy\nCkO+jT0SxiSBYUlABK7yb2N29aNFSJf+lpVaqg5V1njQSsyYxu7vjncwq30jL5My\nodCAjWqdbIUD8Waz9D2qMAIJICiHNi85ZnMOK0+lvBlncsYa9oAQFcpBT9kD/qyQ\nTzIjEIWz9hbmD29cuv3I+T4NLpJDtbUgCDbTMfKzHFo/JVtWZqubp3dktK6tNs/0\nTdm+VKO+O+X5L30tsYijn8GRWDsW5SVE4rBlY9Y4awLNyfYr9lK7ENHR8PXsHIZG\nz7z47b9mfXlSurbyDE75bFE+SlACmr3mMsJDJ2Yd7Ysv9LoaeOUFBXwXsFk