cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/b9a797ecd68900e9687beb6f09869d52a97eff9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:30:15Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:30:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: sync the `__sx` base-styling model and `style-props-to-sx` codemod from Tonic One (#1213)\n\n* refactor(react): route component base styling through the internal `__sx` channel\n\nSyncs Tonic UI with the `__sx` base-styling model already shipped in Tonic One,\nso a component''s own base styling structurally loses to a consumer override no\nmatter which CSS property either touches.\n\n- `useSlot` composes an incoming `__sx` via `composeSx` (mirroring how it merges\n  `ref`), instead of letting `slotProps.__sx` silently replace the base.\n- `Button`/`ButtonBase`, the `Input` family (`Input`, `InputBase`,\n  `InputControl`, `InputGroupAppend`, `InputGroupPrepend`), and `MenuButton`\n  move their base styling off style-prop spreads / the Emotion `css` prop and\n  onto `__sx`, folded after `{...rest}` with `composeSx(styleProps, __sxProp)`.\n- `MenuButton` now injects its hover/active override through the child `Button`''s\n  `__sx` rather than hand-merging it onto `css`; the override is expressed as the\n  `text.primary` token so color mode and `useCSSVariables` both resolve it.\n- Input in-group rules are folded into their style hooks (`getInputGroupSx`),\n  and the append/prepend child-radius rules stay in their hooks.\n\nBehavior is unchanged: every regenerated snapshot is a tier reorder, verified by\ncomparing the computed (last-wins) declarations per Emotion class against the\nprevious output. Adds cascade-order proof tests for `MenuButton` and\n`PaginationItem`, and an `InputGroup` regression test for the nested in-group\nradius rules (no previous test rendered them).\n\nThe `Menu`/`Dropdown`/`Tabs` snapshots additionally gain the `MenuItem` disabled\nvariant''s own class, and the `Menu` snapshot now emits the menu button''s\nhover/active override -- previously produced via the `css` prop.\n\n* feat(react): add the `slots` API to `Scrollbar` and route its styling through `__sx`\n\n`Scrollbar` was the last configurable part in the library without a slot API, and\nits two ad-hoc props (`scrollViewProps`, `scrollViewRef`) could not express an\nelement swap even though the internal `ScrollView` owns a ref contract the\ncomponent''s measurement logic depends on.\n\n- Adds `slots`/`slotProps` for `root`, `scrollView`, `horizontalTrack`,\n  `verticalTrack`, `horizontalThumb`, and `verticalThumb`. Element swap applies\n  in default mode; in render-prop mode the part components stay exposed and\n  `slotProps` still flows through the getters.\n- Deprecates `scrollViewProps` -> `slotProps.scrollView` and `scrollViewRef` ->\n  `slotProps.scrollView.ref` (both still work, with a `warnDeprecatedProps`\n  warning).\n- Routes every base style through `__sx`: the root folds the incoming component\n  `__sx` via `composeSx`, the scroll view folds the incoming\n  `scrollViewProps.__sx`, and the tracks/thumbs pass their style directly.\n- Moves the scrollbar-hiding base (`::-webkit-scrollbar`, `msOverflowStyle`,\n  `scrollbarWidth`) into the scroll view style. This also fixes\n  `-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch`, which was previously discarded as a\n  non-forwarded plain prop.\n- Renames the scrollbar style hooks to the `useScrollbar*` namespace and makes\n  `ScrollView` a passthrough.\n\n* docs(react-docs): document the Scrollbar slots API\n\nMigrates the React Virtuoso recipe to `slotProps.scrollView` and documents the\nnew `slots`/`slotProps` props alongside the `scrollViewProps`/`scrollViewRef`\ndeprecations.\n\n* feat(codemod): resolve same-file wrappers and flag unresolvable ones in `style-props-to-sx`\n\nPorted from the Tonic One transform, adapted to Tonic UI''s package names and\nkeeping this repo''s (larger) protected-prop list.\n\n- `resolveLocalWrapper` resolves a wrapper declared in the *same file* as its\n  usage, where there is no import statement to walk; it recurses through chained\n  same-file hops and falls back to the cross-file resolver.\n- A JSX tag whose wrapper cannot be resolved is now flagged with a\n  `console.warn` when it carries style-prop-like attributes, instead of being\n  skipped silently and looking like \"nothing to convert\".\n- DOM intrinsic tags (lowercase) are skipped outright -- `width`/`height` on\n  `<img>`/`<svg>` are real HTML attributes, not an unresolved wrapper.\n- `Box`/`Flex`/`Grid`/`Stack`/`StackItem`/`Space` are no longer whole-component\n  exempt: their flat style props convert like any other component''s. This is a\n  tooling/convention change only -- flat style props keep working at runtime.\n- Fixes the README''s `import-react-icons` path (`react/v2`, not `react/v2.0.0`),\n  which did not match the on-disk directory the tests use.\n\n* docs: record the `__sx` styling-channel model and sync the sx/slots skills\n\n- Adds `CONTEXT.md`, the shared styling-channel glossary (`__sx`, style props,\n  pseudo props, `sx`) and the distinctions the rules depend on.\n- Adds the ADRs the guidance rests on: `__sx` as the universal internal base\n  channel, the `Scrollbar`/`useSlot` `__sx`-composition decision, and the\n  `__sx`-regression test methodology. Updates the transition-style ADR to\n  `composeSx`.\n- Brings the `tonic-ui-sx` and `tonic-ui-slots` skills up to date with the\n  shipped behavior, and fixes their dangling references (`CONTEXT.md`, the\n  migration-plan filename, the `tonic-ui-slots` link) and stale `mergeSx` naming.\n- Adds the execution plan for this sync, including the verification record and\n  the Input in-group regression it caught.\n\n* chore(changeset): add the release note for the `__sx` sync (#1213)","tree":{"sha":"cffd39e228c7d8e3c90dae5a98ec99d684777a87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/cffd39e228c7d8e3c90dae5a98ec99d684777a87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/b9a797ecd68900e9687beb6f09869d52a97eff9b","verification":{"payload":"tree cffd39e228c7d8e3c90dae5a98ec99d684777a87\nparent 0cc04f995d34da6eeb1c73dec172f97129b6a81b\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1791358215 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791358215 +0800\n\nfeat: sync the `__sx` base-styling model and `style-props-to-sx` codemod from Tonic One (#1213)\n\n* refactor(react): route component base styling through the internal `__sx` channel\n\nSyncs Tonic UI with the `__sx` base-styling model already shipped in Tonic One,\nso a component''s own base styling structurally loses to a consumer override no\nmatter which CSS property either touches.\n\n- `useSlot` composes an incoming `__sx` via `composeSx` (mirroring how it merges\n  `ref`), instead of letting `slotProps.__sx` silently replace the base.\n- `Button`/`ButtonBase`, the `Input` family (`Input`, `InputBase`,\n  `InputControl`, `InputGroupAppend`, `InputGroupPrepend`), and `MenuButton`\n  move their base styling off style-prop spreads / the Emotion `css` prop and\n  onto `__sx`, folded after `{...rest}` with `composeSx(styleProps, __sxProp)`.\n- `MenuButton` now injects its hover/active override through the child `Button`''s\n  `__sx` rather than hand-merging it onto `css`; the override is expressed as the\n  `text.primary` token so color mode and `useCSSVariables` both resolve it.\n- Input in-group rules are folded into their style hooks (`getInputGroupSx`),\n  and the append/prepend child-radius rules stay in their hooks.\n\nBehavior is unchanged: every regenerated snapshot is a tier reorder, verified by\ncomparing the computed (last-wins) declarations per Emotion class against the\nprevious output. Adds cascade-order proof tests for `MenuButton` and\n`PaginationItem`, and an `InputGroup` regression test for the nested in-group\nradius rules (no previous test rendered them).\n\nThe `Menu`/`Dropdown`/`Tabs` snapshots additionally gain the `MenuItem` disabled\nvariant''s own class, and the `Menu` snapshot now emits the menu button''s\nhover/active override -- previously produced via the `css` prop.\n\n* feat(react): add the `slots` API to `Scrollbar` and route its styling through `__sx`\n\n`Scrollbar` was the last configurable part in the library without a slot API, and\nits two ad-hoc props (`scrollViewProps`, `scrollViewRef`) could not express an\nelement swap even though the internal `ScrollView` owns a ref contract the\ncomponent''s measurement logic depends on.\n\n- Adds `slots`/`slotProps` for `root`, `scrollView`, `horizontalTrack`,\n  `verticalTrack`, `horizontalThumb`, and `verticalThumb`. Element swap applies\n  in default mode; in render-prop mode the part components stay exposed and\n  `slotProps` still flows through the getters.\n- Deprecates `scrollViewProps` -> `slotProps.scrollView` and `scrollViewRef` ->\n  `slotProps.scrollView.ref` (both still work, with a `warnDeprecatedProps`\n  warning).\n- Routes every base style through `__sx`: the root folds the incoming component\n  `__sx` via `composeSx`, the scroll view folds the incoming\n  `scrollViewProps.__sx`, and the tracks/thumbs pass their style directly.\n- Moves the scrollbar-hiding base (`::-webkit-scrollbar`, `msOverflowStyle`,\n  `scrollbarWidth`) into the scroll view style. This also fixes\n  `-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch`, which was previously discarded as a\n  non-forwarded plain prop.\n- Renames the scrollbar style hooks to the `useScrollbar*` namespace and makes\n  `ScrollView` a passthrough.\n\n* docs(react-docs): document the Scrollbar slots API\n\nMigrates the React Virtuoso recipe to `slotProps.scrollView` and documents the\nnew `slots`/`slotProps` props alongside the `scrollViewProps`/`scrollViewRef`\ndeprecations.\n\n* feat(codemod): resolve same-file wrappers and flag unresolvable ones in `style-props-to-sx`\n\nPorted from the Tonic One transform, adapted to Tonic UI''s package names and\nkeeping this repo''s (larger) protected-prop list.\n\n- `resolveLocalWrapper` resolves a wrapper declared in the *same file* as its\n  usage, where there is no import statement to walk; it recurses through chained\n  same-file hops and falls back to the cross-file resolver.\n- A JSX tag whose wrapper cannot be resolved is now flagged with a\n  `console.warn` when it carries style-prop-like attributes, instead of being\n  skipped silently and looking like \"nothing to convert\".\n- DOM intrinsic tags (lowercase) are skipped outright -- `width`/`height` on\n  `<img>`/`<svg>` are real HTML attributes, not an unresolved wrapper.\n- `Box`/`Flex`/`Grid`/`Stack`/`StackItem`/`Space` are no longer whole-component\n  exempt: their flat style props convert like any other component''s. This is a\n  tooling/convention change only -- flat style props keep working at runtime.\n- Fixes the README''s `import-react-icons` path (`react/v2`, not `react/v2.0.0`),\n  which did not match the on-disk directory the tests use.\n\n* docs: record the `__sx` styling-channel model and sync the sx/slots skills\n\n- Adds `CONTEXT.md`, the shared styling-channel glossary (`__sx`, style props,\n  pseudo props, `sx`) and the distinctions the rules depend on.\n- Adds the ADRs the guidance rests on: `__sx` as the universal internal base\n  channel, the `Scrollbar`/`useSlot` `__sx`-composition decision, and the\n  `__sx`-regression test methodology. Updates the transition-style ADR to\n  `composeSx`.\n- Brings the `tonic-ui-sx` and `tonic-ui-slots` skills up to date with the\n  shipped behavior, and fixes their dangling references (`CONTEXT.md`, the\n  migration-plan filename, the `tonic-ui-slots` link) and stale `mergeSx` naming.\n- Adds the execution plan for this sync, including the verification record and\n  the Input in-group regression it caught.\n\n* chore(changeset): add the release note for the `__sx` sync (#1213)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxfUHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAShcQAD7VCmLEvIhqeO5mtitedHhe\n8z6GMT8DNJpcLY6CLduEY4aYc+pZ2Vg4Gg7QbGM/5+ECZDuzTIXuAdrES7fzl1+I\n8xUMWun8jbHnzxfvk9mNfY2GV9hoIO9ClqnNeYSWbz/LIQY5r28J+svkqXo69r7D\nBPVebEj8HY4G0zwACDNmxmiR2arPkdC20Z6bb8jpZ9sKjJX93zZrNg6syNiJkv98\nmG5kY49ELQAnDOoAQlJbjWExeAeFkJXWrApAPxsJfloYrrghPldCVXB+375nVy5W\nbskqNHuKIRNRID+0L+NI1zjFyFlnDIRCI0zAGpfOzlzzYdzAOpUaqiAoM3IAinZI\nK2rmXVExPEBVk2/tJNx2TRTyXxKRog+0811tiasVbfeHFIL3yk3hpJZuw0xnN0yB\nc6r9EPD6PK4N7YKjC12wD/8c12zJNCLRbOqdpJcfvT07H/IdILyXW+0Si+mcZRJC\ncKHYQP6sP0TY6eIw57Qbm/GlAyT9YZMgjeTlWX7mmvAQxyBbsz4KqajaxaA/i7bt\nBa8CK0MTGdMgoGCuqDitIBKYGd8zu1hMFVJuy+HYhWh9uJ7GGtvAT68fSfQHd8NM\nJP6D0R5JwlI7tV0X5IJCBOrA5IKOnYaa8QJOVK5CcVjoFiG4zWokrgNI2Fzonm0A\nfN5t/mVOug5odxvSpMA2\n=j/WA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T07:30:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/b9a797ecd68900e9687beb6f09869d52a97eff9b","node_id":"C_kwDODfyux9oAKGI5YTc5N2VjZDY4OTAwZTk2ODdiZWI2ZjA5ODY5ZDUyYTk3ZWZmOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/0cc04f995d34da6eeb1c73dec172f97129b6a81b","sha":"0cc04f995d34da6eeb1c73dec172f97129b6a81b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/0cc04f995d34da6eeb1c73dec172f97129b6a81b"}],"sha":"b9a797ecd68900e9687beb6f09869d52a97eff9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/b9a797ecd68900e9687beb6f09869d52a97eff9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/447801?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/0cc04f995d34da6eeb1c73dec172f97129b6a81b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:23:57Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:23:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(react/popper): stop recreating the popper instance when modifiers are rebuilt (#1210)\n\n* fix(react/popper): stop recreating the popper instance when modifiers are rebuilt\n\n`Popper` built its modifier array into `setupPopper`''s dependency list, and\nevery `Popper`-based overlay passes that array inline. `modifiers={[...a, ...b]}`\nis a new array every render, so `setupPopper` changed identity, so the\n`refUpdater` handed to the popper element changed identity, so React detached\nand re-attached that ref on every parent render. Each call destroyed the\ninstance, created a new one, and forced an update — and a new instance\nre-installs the `observePopperResize` observer, whose callback calls\n`instance.update()`, which reports a placement through `setPlacementState`. On a\n`flip`-enabled overlay that surfaces as React''s `Maximum update depth exceeded`\n(#185).\n\n`Popper` now compares the incoming `modifiers` by value and keeps the previous\narray while the contents are unchanged. A render that rebuilds the array — and\nrebuilds each modifier object with it, as `{ name: ''offset'', options: { offset:\n[0, 8] } }` does — no longer recreates the instance. A real change still\nrecreates it: `enabled`, `options`, `fn`, `effect`, and modifier order are all\ncompared.\n\nRecursion stops at plain objects and arrays; functions (`fn`, `effect`), DOM\nnodes (`options.element` for the arrow), and class instances are compared by\nreference. A generic deep comparison is wrong here: two distinct DOM nodes are\nstructurally similar and `lodash/isEqual` reports them as equal, while\n`fast-equals` — what `micro-memoize`''s `isKeyItemEqual: ''deep''` uses — overflows\nthe stack on a node whose `parentNode` points back at itself. A `WeakMap` of\nin-progress pairs terminates self-referencing plain objects.\n\n`Popper.test.js` gains two cases against the mocked popper.js: a re-render that\nrebuilds the `modifiers` array inline (with fresh modifier objects) must not\nrecreate the instance, and a real change — `enabled` differing, or the modifier\norder differing — must recreate it. The first fails on the previous commit with\nthree creations for three renders.\n\n`MenuContent.popperStability.test.js` reproduces the loop one layer up, where it\nwas reported: a `MenuContent` whose parent re-renders must keep a single popper\ninstance. `MenuContent` is the component that re-wraps the array\n(`[...popperModifiers, ...ensureArray(popperSlotProps?.modifiers)]`), so it is\nthe closest test to the reported symptom. jsdom has no layout, so a fake popper\ninstance is used and the churn is driven by the ref lifecycle, not geometry.\nIt fails on the previous commit with six creations for six renders.\n\n`OverlayModifiers.test.js` covers the same contract at each Popper-based content\nboundary: `AutocompleteList`, `DatePickerContent`, `MenuContent`,\n`SubmenuContent`, `PopoverContent`, and `TooltipContent` now preserve their\nmerged modifier arrays while both the component defaults and consumer-supplied\nmodifiers remain unchanged, so custom Popper slots receive stable modifier\nreferences during unrelated parent renders.\n\n* chore(changeset): add the popper modifiers stability entry\n\n* Update version type for @tonic-ui/react\n\nChanged version from minor to patch for @tonic-ui/react.","tree":{"sha":"db65a5e47a9aa5616d760e44f9bca30aff94d78e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/db65a5e47a9aa5616d760e44f9bca30aff94d78e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/0cc04f995d34da6eeb1c73dec172f97129b6a81b","verification":{"payload":"tree db65a5e47a9aa5616d760e44f9bca30aff94d78e\nparent e9a6136958cd6a75133ebb18e0192bc193e111c3\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1791275037 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791275037 +0800\n\nfix(react/popper): stop recreating the popper instance when modifiers are rebuilt (#1210)\n\n* fix(react/popper): stop recreating the popper instance when modifiers are rebuilt\n\n`Popper` built its modifier array into `setupPopper`''s dependency list, and\nevery `Popper`-based overlay passes that array inline. `modifiers={[...a, ...b]}`\nis a new array every render, so `setupPopper` changed identity, so the\n`refUpdater` handed to the popper element changed identity, so React detached\nand re-attached that ref on every parent render. Each call destroyed the\ninstance, created a new one, and forced an update — and a new instance\nre-installs the `observePopperResize` observer, whose callback calls\n`instance.update()`, which reports a placement through `setPlacementState`. On a\n`flip`-enabled overlay that surfaces as React''s `Maximum update depth exceeded`\n(#185).\n\n`Popper` now compares the incoming `modifiers` by value and keeps the previous\narray while the contents are unchanged. A render that rebuilds the array — and\nrebuilds each modifier object with it, as `{ name: ''offset'', options: { offset:\n[0, 8] } }` does — no longer recreates the instance. A real change still\nrecreates it: `enabled`, `options`, `fn`, `effect`, and modifier order are all\ncompared.\n\nRecursion stops at plain objects and arrays; functions (`fn`, `effect`), DOM\nnodes (`options.element` for the arrow), and class instances are compared by\nreference. A generic deep comparison is wrong here: two distinct DOM nodes are\nstructurally similar and `lodash/isEqual` reports them as equal, while\n`fast-equals` — what `micro-memoize`''s `isKeyItemEqual: ''deep''` uses — overflows\nthe stack on a node whose `parentNode` points back at itself. A `WeakMap` of\nin-progress pairs terminates self-referencing plain objects.\n\n`Popper.test.js` gains two cases against the mocked popper.js: a re-render that\nrebuilds the `modifiers` array inline (with fresh modifier objects) must not\nrecreate the instance, and a real change — `enabled` differing, or the modifier\norder differing — must recreate it. The first fails on the previous commit with\nthree creations for three renders.\n\n`MenuContent.popperStability.test.js` reproduces the loop one layer up, where it\nwas reported: a `MenuContent` whose parent re-renders must keep a single popper\ninstance. `MenuContent` is the component that re-wraps the array\n(`[...popperModifiers, ...ensureArray(popperSlotProps?.modifiers)]`), so it is\nthe closest test to the reported symptom. jsdom has no layout, so a fake popper\ninstance is used and the churn is driven by the ref lifecycle, not geometry.\nIt fails on the previous commit with six creations for six renders.\n\n`OverlayModifiers.test.js` covers the same contract at each Popper-based content\nboundary: `AutocompleteList`, `DatePickerContent`, `MenuContent`,\n`SubmenuContent`, `PopoverContent`, and `TooltipContent` now preserve their\nmerged modifier arrays while both the component defaults and consumer-supplied\nmodifiers remain unchanged, so custom Popper slots receive stable modifier\nreferences during unrelated parent renders.\n\n* chore(changeset): add the popper modifiers stability entry\n\n* Update version type for @tonic-ui/react\n\nChanged version from minor to patch for @tonic-ui/react.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxLAdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/t4QAAXYizCQPkIbbe8VYdJP/KC1\nPcie03nmRH/u+P/tgulxyFBIsqV9k473Hd00Ga2VV8M7xHagBKgkAMMIrgkOi78E\nWlJFNyxc5ZJtMaiuF1OK+3DohhPvbsijMCNTEEGo2YLTHX8hXjk+HjZFPgR/pamo\nU5mfbnUKNMJPtgDtFUp9OsAzVYKF/ea2LUnL8A45jCTG/Us5iSD19ATA4lSAmVqD\ngDPSZ2CpW6arxAg4NPjCIUEvTjK1P0BAxgDH+F6rKekctE85RP4LliKXoYgqmLGA\nKIOkuJX3ecc/pO5x4TE3JwHKJ0Q4mviHozFreMD/G2N6e23EsdHkwpTwgl8Z0jyb\n