"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/4fceaa868b26844f1372e1eb83436e20686028c8","node_id":"C_kwDODfyux9oAKDRmY2VhYTg2OGIyNjg0NGYxMzcyZTFlYjgzNDM2ZTIwNjg2MDI4Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/cc807876d88cb32960402fa2d13eb850503ef536","sha":"cc807876d88cb32960402fa2d13eb850503ef536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/cc807876d88cb32960402fa2d13eb850503ef536"}],"sha":"4fceaa868b26844f1372e1eb83436e20686028c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/4fceaa868b26844f1372e1eb83436e20686028c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/447801?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/cc807876d88cb32960402fa2d13eb850503ef536/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:35:02Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:35:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(react-docs): add the v2 to v3 migration guide and repair docs navigation (#1198)\n\n* docs: migrating color tokens from v2 to v3\n\n* docs(react-docs): add the v2 to v3 migration guide\n\nAdd a migration guide covering the consumer-visible changes between\n`@tonic-ui/react` v2 and v3:\n\n- package updates: the React floor rises to ^18.3.0||^19, and\n  `@emotion/react` / `@emotion/styled` move from dependencies to\n  peerDependencies, so consumers must install them.\n- app setup: `useCSSBaseline`/`useCSSVariables` casing, the stable-theme\n  requirement, the `createTheme` `cssVariables` option change, and\n  `useTheme` returning `toColorMode()`.\n- breaking changes: `sx` array merging is now per-declaration,\n  `Popper`''s render prop adds `computedPlacement`, and `Box` gains the\n  internal `__sx` base-style channel.\n- component changes: `AutocompleteList` moves to `slots`/`slotProps`,\n  plus the new `Dropdown*` components and `CSSVariables` export.\n- theme changes: the v2 token layer is retained but colliding names\n  change value (radii, fonts, breakpoints).\n- a migration checklist.\n\nPoint the migrations index at the newest guide, and fix the color token\npage''s two dangling links to the guide it references.\n\n* docs(react-docs): register the v2 to v3 migration pages in llms.txt\n\nAdd the two new migration pages to the Migrations section so the MCP\nserver and other LLM consumers can discover them.\n\n* docs(react-docs): refresh the Migrations, Experiments, and Theme nav entries\n\n- Drop `NEW` from Experiments; it is no longer new.\n- Add `NEW` to Migrations, and to the color token and v2 to v3 guides.\n- List `Migrating from v2 to v3` in the Migrations section.\n- Add `NEW` and a `DESIGN TOKENS` heading to Theme, so the token pages\n  are grouped the way they are in Tonic One.\n\n* docs(react-docs): fix the theme page paths in llms.txt\n\nThe theme entries used kebab-case paths (`theme/font-sizes`) and the\npage titles as labels, but the pages live at camelCase paths\n(`theme/fontSizes`). Retarget all five dead links and drop the\n`letter-spacings` entry, which has no page.\n\n* docs(react-docs): repair broken internal links and stray brand names\n\nFix links that resolved to a non-existent page or anchor:\n\n- date-picker: `../../components/input-control` did not resolve.\n- spinner: `./progress` pointed at a sibling, not `components/progress`.\n- micro-frontend: `../environment` is under `components/`.\n- documentation-site: link `patterns/` to a page that exists, and\n  `playground` from the docs root.\n- v0-to-v1: `hooks/use-toggle` is `hooks/useToggle`.\n- v1-to-v2: retarget the removed `#severity-deprecated` and\n  `#chart-deprecated` anchors, the missing `#recommended-configuration`\n  anchor, and `date-pickers/calendar` (now `date-calendar`).\n\nAlso add the missing `installation-for-pr-builds` entry to llms.txt, and\ncorrect two entries that still called this product Tonic One.\n\n* fix(react-docs): link style-prop theme scales to their real page paths\n\n`update-style-props.mjs` kebab-cased the theme scale name when building\nthe `Theme Key` link, so it emitted `theme/font-sizes` while the page\nlives at `theme/fontSizes`. It also linked `letterSpacings`, which has no\ntheme page at all.\n\nUse the scale name verbatim and only link a scale whose page exists, so\nthe generated style-props page no longer contains dead links.\n\n* fix(react/theme): correct the product name in the createTheme warning\n\nThe `cssVariables` boolean warning prefixed its message with `[Tonic One]`,\nwhich is the wrong product. Use `[Tonic UI]`.\n\n* docs(react-docs): use the correct DateCalendar name in the v1 to v2 guide\n\nThe date pickers section linked to `date-pickers/date-calendar`, whose page\ntitle is `DateCalendar`, but the surrounding prose called it `Calendar`.\n`Calendar` now only exists as a deprecated shim that forwards to\n`DateCalendar`, so name the component correctly.\n\n* docs(react-docs): drop the misleading recommended configuration link\n\nThe deprecation notice linked `recommended configuration` to\n`#color-style`, which is just the section heading this notice sits\nunder -- not a configuration reference. Remove the link and keep the\nphrase as plain text.\n\n* revert(react-docs): leave the v1 to v2 migration guide unchanged\n\n`migrating-from-v1-to-v2` documents the v1 to v2 upgrade, so it is out of\nscope for the v2 to v3 work on this branch. Restore it to its state on\n`main`, reverting the link repairs, the `DateCalendar` rename, and the\nrecommended-configuration link removal.\n\n* revert(react-docs): leave the v0 to v1 migration guide unchanged\n\n`migrating-from-v0-to-v1` documents the v0 to v1 upgrade, so it is out of\nscope for the v2 to v3 work on this branch. Restore it to its state on\n`main`.\n\n* docs(react-docs): retarget the dropdown items link label\n\nThe `items` prop table linked `#dropdown-items` but labelled it\n\"Advanced configuration\", a section that does not exist on the page.\n`#dropdown-items` is the `## Dropdown items` heading, and the usage\nsection above already calls it \"Dropdown items\".\n\n* docs(react-docs): separate the Autocomplete and Dropdown entries in llms.txt\n\nEvery other entry is separated by a blank line; these two ran together.\n\n* docs(react-docs): spell the parent path explicitly in the color-style link\n\n`..#default-color-values` and `../#default-color-values` resolve to the\nsame URL, but the former is the only such link in the docs and reads as a\ntypo next to the repo''s `../<path>` convention.","tree":{"sha":"af2e1cdd464a8cdea5ad4f3823a6c2cb703c1f58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/af2e1cdd464a8cdea5ad4f3823a6c2cb703c1f58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/cc807876d88cb32960402fa2d13eb850503ef536","verification":{"payload":"tree af2e1cdd464a8cdea5ad4f3823a6c2cb703c1f58\nparent 14b8199184b6bcdea69f895348d27d6836493d1b\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1789742102 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789742102 +0800\n\ndocs(react-docs): add the v2 to v3 migration guide and repair docs navigation (#1198)\n\n* docs: migrating color tokens from v2 to v3\n\n* docs(react-docs): add the v2 to v3 migration guide\n\nAdd a migration guide covering the consumer-visible changes between\n`@tonic-ui/react` v2 and v3:\n\n- package updates: the React floor rises to ^18.3.0||^19, and\n  `@emotion/react` / `@emotion/styled` move from dependencies to\n  peerDependencies, so consumers must install them.\n- app setup: `useCSSBaseline`/`useCSSVariables` casing, the stable-theme\n  requirement, the `createTheme` `cssVariables` option change, and\n  `useTheme` returning `toColorMode()`.\n- breaking changes: `sx` array merging is now per-declaration,\n  `Popper`''s render prop adds `computedPlacement`, and `Box` gains the\n  internal `__sx` base-style channel.\n- component changes: `AutocompleteList` moves to `slots`/`slotProps`,\n  plus the new `Dropdown*` components and `CSSVariables` export.\n- theme changes: the v2 token layer is retained but colliding names\n  change value (radii, fonts, breakpoints).\n- a migration checklist.\n\nPoint the migrations index at the newest guide, and fix the color token\npage''s two dangling links to the guide it references.\n\n* docs(react-docs): register the v2 to v3 migration pages in llms.txt\n\nAdd the two new migration pages to the Migrations section so the MCP\nserver and other LLM consumers can discover them.\n\n* docs(react-docs): refresh the Migrations, Experiments, and Theme nav entries\n\n- Drop `NEW` from Experiments; it is no longer new.\n- Add `NEW` to Migrations, and to the color token and v2 to v3 guides.\n- List `Migrating from v2 to v3` in the Migrations section.\n- Add `NEW` and a `DESIGN TOKENS` heading to Theme, so the token pages\n  are grouped the way they are in Tonic One.\n\n* docs(react-docs): fix the theme page paths in llms.txt\n\nThe theme entries used kebab-case paths (`theme/font-sizes`) and the\npage titles as labels, but the pages live at camelCase paths\n(`theme/fontSizes`). Retarget all five dead links and drop the\n`letter-spacings` entry, which has no page.\n\n* docs(react-docs): repair broken internal links and stray brand names\n\nFix links that resolved to a non-existent page or anchor:\n\n- date-picker: `../../components/input-control` did not resolve.\n- spinner: `./progress` pointed at a sibling, not `components/progress`.\n- micro-frontend: `../environment` is under `components/`.\n- documentation-site: link `patterns/` to a page that exists, and\n  `playground` from the docs root.\n- v0-to-v1: `hooks/use-toggle` is `hooks/useToggle`.\n- v1-to-v2: retarget the removed `#severity-deprecated` and\n  `#chart-deprecated` anchors, the missing `#recommended-configuration`\n  anchor, and `date-pickers/calendar` (now `date-calendar`).\n\nAlso add the missing `installation-for-pr-builds` entry to llms.txt, and\ncorrect two entries that still called this product Tonic One.\n\n* fix(react-docs): link style-prop theme scales to their real page paths\n\n`update-style-props.mjs` kebab-cased the theme scale name when building\nthe `Theme Key` link, so it emitted `theme/font-sizes` while the page\nlives at `theme/fontSizes`. It also linked `letterSpacings`, which has no\ntheme page at all.\n\nUse the scale name verbatim and only link a scale whose page exists, so\nthe generated style-props page no longer contains dead links.\n\n* fix(react/theme): correct the product name in the createTheme warning\n\nThe `cssVariables` boolean warning prefixed its message with `[Tonic One]`,\nwhich is the wrong product. Use `[Tonic UI]`.\n\n* docs(react-docs): use the correct DateCalendar name in the v1 to v2 guide\n\nThe date pickers section linked to `date-pickers/date-calendar`, whose page\ntitle is `DateCalendar`, but the surrounding prose called it `Calendar`.\n`Calendar` now only exists as a deprecated shim that forwards to\n`DateCalendar`, so name the component correctly.\n\n* docs(react-docs): drop the misleading recommended configuration link\n\nThe deprecation notice linked `recommended configuration` to\n`#color-style`, which is just the section heading this notice sits\nunder -- not a configuration reference. Remove the link and keep the\nphrase as plain text.\n\n* revert(react-docs): leave the v1 to v2 migration guide unchanged\n\n`migrating-from-v1-to-v2` documents the v1 to v2 upgrade, so it is out of\nscope for the v2 to v3 work on this branch. Restore it to its state on\n`main`, reverting the link repairs, the `DateCalendar` rename, and the\nrecommended-configuration link removal.\n\n* revert(react-docs): leave the v0 to v1 migration guide unchanged\n\n`migrating-from-v0-to-v1` documents the v0 to v1 upgrade, so it is out of\nscope for the v2 to v3 work on this branch. Restore it to its state on\n`main`.\n\n* docs(react-docs): retarget the dropdown items link label\n\nThe `items` prop table linked `#dropdown-items` but labelled it\n\"Advanced configuration\", a section that does not exist on the page.\n`#dropdown-items` is the `## Dropdown items` heading, and the usage\nsection above already calls it \"Dropdown items\".\n\n* docs(react-docs): separate the Autocomplete and Dropdown entries in llms.txt\n\nEvery other entry is separated by a blank line; these two ran together.\n\n* docs(react-docs): spell the parent path explicitly in the color-style link\n\n`..#default-color-values` and `../#default-color-values` resolve to the\nsame URL, but the former is the only such link in the docs and reads as a\ntypo next to the repo''s `../<path>` convention.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrUwWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8toQAH+G/OR9C5Da+VbHftDoqlmK\n7EjLTaEnDCufeBIWF0ubyHACuk12wsTuRz9bWHn2Z4ezuoZVWtb2ty2qN2I+tBgg\nR7Tj63KTR/sZWSMe9Tk6HAD4K0irdTNMY245jdKiAZPCPjZ9hO5CPcOq5kKLkQZY\nXg+hSI15CTOgkqsSrMk7e0L+uHi1aYg+Q42czKfQGsdtrAr2VUv5ALl6+6mOt7k0\nehbdjTQWCApLVg5Bd1ZTSK2ckFX9qJEbJRLzNnBNQ4IAO5ExXtHtYj7sLW1JH8Jq\nngFBMPphQ+p9Ujk72CtNbp95azB+FFMC61QIWtBJXKcFRNEPksAGHvwPi9T/mu0L\n/CrHgtoAC+83XCDwucM6Gv76awI1QJJA7SyEnsH+lHy+/N69nADLD50PxE+Kg/hP\nvYVGxgJrBvVD5Uv7WYh5TSEuI3oHxEIlEESxWtFBWtDAmpAh9gJ6w4CEdQQMlTKz\ni6vyGPBi2xOWQdhRXQmxnmCFZVvZ0B03eoRdLvBbpCUdE6O2BDk5THi465aT1xJc\ndgReeZD9H1cEuTUJi6etzfTuufmD5DxD26iUQo0EKTRjzFZm6coajzRFnRI9pDjl\nrZvhyV5KD+oDXwrVIQOQTVOPl8cDsFFdU6Ef0cVKImPul1PuhtpPnZUjA9sQ026Q\nOMPamOjMsHIPrnsS2QS0\n=P+OF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T14:35:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/cc807876d88cb32960402fa2d13eb850503ef536","node_id":"C_kwDODfyux9oAKGNjODA3ODc2ZDg4Y2IzMjk2MDQwMmZhMmQxM2ViODUwNTAzZWY1MzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/14b8199184b6bcdea69f895348d27d6836493d1b","sha":"14b8199184b6bcdea69f895348d27d6836493d1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/14b8199184b6bcdea69f895348d27d6836493d1b"}],"sha":"cc807876d88cb32960402fa2d13eb850503ef536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/cc807876d88cb32960402fa2d13eb850503ef536"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/447801?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/14b8199184b6bcdea69f895348d27d6836493d1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:16:19Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:16:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(react/popper): update the popper position after its content resizes (#1207)\n\n* fix(react/popper): update position after the popper content resizes\n\nRe-run the update cycle when the popper element changes size, so an enabled\n`flip` modifier reacts to content that grows after the initial measurement\n(for example a `Collapse` enter transition). The observation lives in an\ninternal modifier effect, so popper.js owns its cleanup, and the constructor\nis read from `useEnvironment().getWindow()` through `useLatestRef` to keep the\nmodifier identity stable across environment re-renders.\n\nAlso:\n- destroy the instance when the popper element is detached without unmounting\n  (`unmountOnExit` without a transition, StrictMode ref replay);\n- keep the consumer placement as the preferred `createPopper` input and report\n  the computed placement to the render function;\n- use a module-level array as the `modifiers` default to stop per-render\n  instance recreation.\n\n* docs(popper): add the first-open flip RCA and fix plan\n\nRecord the source-derived root cause, the corrections found during review\n(controlled placement was not feeding the flipped value back, the referenced\ndropdown demo does not exist in this repository, popper v2 has no autoUpdate),\nthe verified implementation status, and the still-owed browser check.\n\n* fix(react/popper): expose the computed placement separately\n\nThe render function now receives `{ placement, computedPlacement }`. `placement`\nkeeps meaning the preferred placement, so no existing consumer contract changes,\nand `computedPlacement` carries the placement Popper.js actually used.\n\n`Popover` and `Tooltip` read `computedPlacement` for `transformOrigin`, so the\ncontent grows from the edge that faces the trigger. `Grow` animates opacity and\ntransform only and never changes layout size, so the popper box is final before\nthe enter transition starts and the flip is known from the first frame.\n\nAlso:\n- test JSX uses `Box` rather than a raw `div`;\n- the `placement` prop tables for popover, tooltip, autocomplete, menu, submenu\n  and date picker now describe it as the preferred placement.\n\n* docs(popper): update the flip plan and add a handoff note\n\nRecord the final render-prop naming decision, the verified consumer impact\nacross all six Popper-based components, the known gaps left in place, and the\nhandoff note covering the remaining changeset and browser verification.\n\n* chore(changeset): add the popper flip fix entry\n\n* docs(popper): record the PR number and the added changeset\n\n* fix(react/popper): declare the phase the resize modifier needs\n\npopper.js''s `orderModifiers` keeps only modifiers whose `phase` is one of its\nknown phases, so `observePopperResize` was dropped from `state.orderedModifiers`\nbefore `runModifierEffects()` could call its effect. No ResizeObserver was ever\nconstructed and no re-measure happened on content resize.\n\nAdding `phase: ''read''` restores the mechanism. The existing resize test invoked\n`modifier.effect` by hand, so it passed while popper.js was discarding the\nmodifier; the new test runs the real popper.js and asserts the modifier survives\nordering. Deleting the `phase` line makes it fail with the modifier absent.\n\nRead the shared window through `ownerWindow`, matching the convention used by\n`scrollbar/Scrollbar.js`. The `useLatestRef` indirection stays: a direct\n`getWindow` dependency recreates the instance whenever `EnvironmentProvider`''s\n`value` changes identity, which an existing test pins.\n\nBack-ported from the downstream Tonic One fix, which found the defect.\n\n* test(react/popper): pin that Popper renders without a DOM\n\n`Popper` gates every window access behind effects or callbacks, so it renders\nunder `renderToString`. Nothing pinned that, and moving `getWindow()` up to the\nrender scope silently breaks server rendering with `window is not defined`.\n\n* docs(react/popper): explain why `getWindow` is read through a ref\n\n`getWindow` changes identity whenever `EnvironmentProvider`''s `value` is not\nreferentially stable, and the modifier array feeds `setupPopper`''s dependencies,\nso a re-created instance is the cost of listing it directly.\n\n`useEventCallback` is the other candidate in `@tonic-ui/react-hooks`, and it does\nnot work here: it is a ref-boxed callback that throws until a layout effect has\nstored the function, and popper.js runs the modifier effect during the commit\nphase, so reading it there throws \"Cannot call an event handler while\nrendering\". The new test runs the real popper.js through the component''s own\ncommit and pins both failures: dropping the ref recreates the instance, and\nswapping in `useEventCallback` throws.\n\n* docs(popper): correct the docs scope and the test counts\n\nOnly `popover`, `tooltip` and `autocomplete` have a `placement` row in their\nprop table; `Menu` and `DatePicker` document `placement` in prose only. The\nrecords claimed six pages, and the handoff still described the pre-fix test\ncount.\n\n* docs(handoffs): replace the handoff with the next task\n\nThe shipped `flip` fix is now browser-verified, so the handoff no longer needs\nto carry it as outstanding work. It now covers the modifier-array instability\nfound while auditing the six Popper consumers: every overlay rebuilds its popper\ninstance on each parent render because `modifiers` is built inline in JSX, which\ntakes `setupPopper`''s referential stability with it.\n\n* docs(handoffs): scope the modifier-array follow-up away from `TooltipContent`\n\nIts `[getWindow, ...]` dependency is not where the defect lives. A raw `Popover`\nreproduces the same per-render instance recreation with no `getWindow`\ndependency at all, so patching `TooltipContent` would leave the cause intact\neverywhere else. The follow-up now points at `Popper`''s own handling of the\n`modifiers` input, or at leaving it alone.\n\n* fix(react/popper): simplify environment dependency and observer lifecycle\n\n* docs(react-docs): answer the flip question for `Dropdown`\n\n`Dropdown` disables `flip` by default, so the nested slot-props path needed to\nenable it deserves an example rather than only appearing inside the search\nrecipe. Adds a \"Commonly asked questions\" section mirroring the `Popover` page:\na stable trigger inside a scroll viewport where a `top` placement cannot fit, and\na checkbox that turns the modifier on and off so the difference is visible.\n\nThe toggle sits at the top of the viewport on purpose. A centred toggle has room\nabove it, `top` fits, and nothing flips; a comment records that constraint so it\nsurvives later edits.\n\n* docs(react-docs): give the shims a migration heading\n\n`Shims` described a moving-off-a-legacy-API path, not a feature of the current\ncomponent, and the page was the only one in the docs with that heading. Renames\nit to `Migrating from a legacy dropdown API`, matching the `Migrating from vN to\nvN` convention in `pages/migrations`.\n\n`Commonly asked questions` now follows it, so the reference material ends with\nprops and the question-style content stays together.\n\n* docs(react-docs): open the flip example upward\n\nThe example requested a `top` placement inside a scroller and flipped it to\n`bottom`, so the default state opened downward and the flip was invisible unless\nthe checkbox was toggled.\n\nIt now requests `bottom` against a clipping container, which is the case `flip`\nexists for: with the modifier on, the content opens upward and stays whole; with\nit off, the content opens downward and is cut off after the first item. The\n`Scrollbar` is replaced by a plain `overflow: hidden` container, since scrolling\nwas never the point and it made the demo small and fiddly.\n\n* docs(react-docs): derive the flip example geometry from the item list\n\nThe example needs a clipping container that satisfies two opposing constraints:\n`flip` has to fit the whole menu above the toggle, and without `flip` the menu\nhas to overflow below. A hardcoded height can only satisfy both by coincidence,\nand a too-short container silently disables the demonstration — `flip` stops\nbeing able to move the menu at all, so both states look identical.\n\nThe height and padding now come from the item count and the theme tokens that\ngive `MenuItem` its height (`lineHeight.sm` plus `py: ''2x''`), which reproduces\nthe measured 124px panel exactly.\n\nVerified in Chromium: with `flip` on, a requested `bottom` resolves `top` and\nall three items are fully visible; with `flip` off, it stays `bottom` and the\ncontainer shows the first item whole plus most of the second before cutting off.","tree":{"sha":"d68565c50be381f4bbd890901839f2ec2edcac17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/d68565c50be381f4bbd890901839f2ec2edcac17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/14b8199184b6bcdea69f895348d27d6836493d1b","verification":{"payload":"tree d68565c50be381f4bbd890901839f2ec2edcac17\nparent 5f770984d8f2ac675bb8f0e6cb6467e772a43772\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1789712179 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789712179 +0800\n\nfix(react/popper): update the popper position after its content resizes (#1207)\n\n* fix(react/popper): update position after the popper content resizes\n\nRe-run the update cycle when the popper element changes size, so an enabled\n`flip` modifier reacts to content that grows after the initial measurement\n(for example a `Collapse` enter transition). The observation lives in an\ninternal modifier effect, so popper.js owns its cleanup, and the constructor\nis read from `useEnvironment().getWindow()` through `useLatestRef` to keep the\nmodifier identity stable across environment re-renders.\n\nAlso:\n- destroy the instance when the popper element is detached without unmounting\n  (`unmountOnExit` without a transition, StrictMode ref replay);\n- keep the consumer placement as the preferred `createPopper` input and report\n  the computed placement to the render function;\n- use a module-level array as the `modifiers` default to stop per-render\n  instance recreation.\n\n* docs(popper): add the first-open flip RCA and fix plan\n\nRecord the source-derived root cause, the corrections found during review\n(controlled placement was not feeding the flipped value back, the referenced\ndropdown demo does not exist in this repository, popper v2 has no autoUpdate),\nthe verified implementation status, and the still-owed browser check.\n\n* fix(react/popper): expose the computed placement separately\n\nThe render function now receives `{ placement, computedPlacement }`. `placement`\nkeeps meaning the preferred placement, so no existing consumer contract changes,\nand `computedPlacement` carries the placement Popper.js actually used.\n\n`Popover` and `Tooltip` read `computedPlacement` for `transformOrigin`, so the\ncontent grows from the edge that faces the trigger. `Grow` animates opacity and\ntransform only and never changes layout size, so the popper box is final before\nthe enter transition starts and the flip is known from the first frame.\n\nAlso:\n- test JSX uses `Box` rather than a raw `div`;\n- the `placement` prop tables for popover, tooltip, autocomplete, menu, submenu\n  and date picker now describe it as the preferred placement.\n\n* docs(popper): update the flip plan and add a handoff note\n\nRecord the final render-prop naming decision, the verified consumer impact\nacross all six Popper-based components, the known gaps left in place, and the\nhandoff note covering the remaining changeset and browser verification.\n\n* chore(changeset): add the popper flip fix entry\n\n* docs(popper): record the PR number and the added changeset\n\n* fix(react/popper): declare the phase the resize modifier needs\n\npopper.js''s `orderModifiers` keeps only modifiers whose `phase` is one of its\nknown phases, so `observePopperResize` was dropped from `state.orderedModifiers`\nbefore `runModifierEffects()` could call its effect. No ResizeObserver was ever\nconstructed and no re-measure happened on content resize.\n\nAdding `phase: ''read''` restores the mechanism. The existing resize test invoked\n`modifier.effect` by hand, so it passed while popper.js was discarding the\nmodifier; the new test runs the real popper.js and asserts the modifier survives\nordering. Deleting the `phase` line makes it fail with the modifier absent.\n\nRead the shared window through `ownerWindow`, matching the convention used by\n`scrollbar/Scrollbar.js`. The `useLatestRef` indirection stays: a direct\n`getWindow` dependency recreates the instance whenever `EnvironmentProvider`''s\n`value` changes identity, which an existing test pins.\n\nBack-ported from the downstream Tonic One fix, which found the defect.\n\n* test(react/popper): pin that Popper renders without a DOM\n\n`Popper` gates every window access behind effects or callbacks, so it renders\nunder `renderToString`. Nothing pinned that, and moving `getWindow()` up to the\nrender scope silently breaks server rendering with `window is not defined`.\n\n* docs(react/popper): explain why `getWindow` is read through a ref\n\n`getWindow` changes identity whenever `EnvironmentProvider`''s `value` is not\nreferentially stable, and the modifier array feeds `setupPopper`''s dependencies,\nso a re-created instance is the cost of listing it directly.\n\n`useEventCallback` is the other candidate in `@tonic-ui/react-hooks`, and it does\nnot work here: it is a ref-boxed callback that throws until a layout effect has\nstored the function, and popper.js runs the modifier effect during the commit\nphase, so reading it there throws \"Cannot call an event handler while\nrendering\". The new test runs the real popper.js through the component''s own\ncommit and pins both failures: dropping the ref recreates the instance, and\nswapping in `useEventCallback` throws.\n\n* docs(popper): correct the docs scope and the test counts\n\nOnly `popover`, `tooltip` and `autocomplete` have a `placement` row in their\nprop table; `Menu` and `DatePicker` document `placement` in prose only. The\nrecords claimed six pages, and the handoff still described the pre-fix test\ncount.\n\n* docs(handoffs): replace the handoff with the next task\n\nThe shipped `flip` fix is now browser-verified, so the handoff no longer needs\nto carry it as outstanding work. It now covers the modifier-array instability\nfound while auditing the six Popper consumers: every overlay rebuilds its popper\ninstance on each parent render because `modifiers` is built inline in JSX, which\ntakes `setupPopper`''s referential stability with it.\n\n* docs(handoffs): scope the modifier-array follow-up away from `TooltipContent`\n\nIts `[getWindow, ...]` dependency is not where the defect lives. A raw `Popover`\nreproduces the same per-render instance recreation with no `getWindow`\ndependency at all, so patching `TooltipContent` would leave the cause intact\neverywhere else. The follow-up now points at `Popper`''s own handling of the\n`modifiers` input, or at leaving it alone.\n\n* fix(react/popper): simplify environment dependency and observer lifecycle\n\n* docs(react-docs): answer the flip question for `Dropdown`\n\n`Dropdown` disables `flip` by default, so the nested slot-props path needed to\nenable it deserves an example rather than only appearing inside the search\nrecipe. Adds a \"Commonly asked questions\" section mirroring the `Popover` page:\na stable trigger inside a scroll viewport where a `top` placement cannot fit, and\na checkbox that turns the modifier on and off so the difference is visible.\n\nThe toggle sits at the top of the viewport on purpose. A centred toggle has room\nabove it, `top` fits, and nothing flips; a comment records that constraint so it\nsurvives later edits.\n\n* docs(react-docs): give the shims a migration heading\n\n`Shims` described a moving-off-a-legacy-API path, not a feature of the current\ncomponent, and the page was the only one in the docs with that heading. Renames\nit to `Migrating from a legacy dropdown API`, matching the `Migrating from vN to\nvN` convention in `pages/migrations`.\n\n`Commonly asked questions` now follows it, so the reference material ends with\nprops and the question-style content stays together.\n\n* docs(react-docs): open the flip example upward\n\nThe example requested a `top` placement inside a scroller and flipped it to\n`bottom`, so the default state opened downward and the flip was invisible unless\nthe checkbox was toggled.\n\nIt now requests `bottom` against a clipping container, which is the case `flip`\nexists for: with the modifier on, the content opens upward and stays whole; with\nit off, the content opens downward and is cut off after the first item. The\n`Scrollbar` is replaced by a plain `overflow: hidden` container, since scrolling\nwas never the point and it made the demo small and fiddly.\n\n* docs(react-docs): derive the flip example geometry from the item list\n\nThe example needs a clipping container that satisfies two opposing constraints:\n`flip` has to fit the whole menu above the toggle, and without `flip` the menu\nhas to overflow below. A hardcoded height can only satisfy both by coincidence,\nand a too-short container silently disables the demonstration — `flip` stops\nbeing able to move the menu at all, so both states look identical.\n\nThe height and padding now come from the item count and the theme tokens that\ngive `MenuItem` its height (`lineHeight.sm` plus `py: ''2x''`), which reproduces\nthe measured 124px panel exactly.\n\nVerified in Chromium: with `flip` on, a requested `bottom` resolves `top` and\nall three items are fully visible; with `flip` off, it stays `bottom` and the\ncontainer shows the first item whole plus most of the second before cutting off.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrNczCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkyMQACvXe/9Qe70K0gPmf1CaXeYd\n6le+5Gg/8yfri8XxK/2a267xJJh/s3Hr18gprxRXS1JxYFcZh50i54hJu7oMWyRy\nQ6n+9w2b+/VkY2s0/Eh6Ujnm/Hl9LZsSnTzrVtDjkMReYvAP0ZdIEB6