ontend/tonic-ui/commits/cc01d68c9a71db5fec7a725aea7e90e1e0061e41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/447801?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/79e59835bb1718291fceb6eba6a490baa49015d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T12:59:39Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T12:59:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): source pr-preview tooling scripts from a trusted ref (#1186)\n\n* fix(ci): source pr-preview tooling scripts from a trusted ref\n\nThe job checks out the PR''s own head ref, then later steps run\nscripts/pr-preview/*.sh and scripts/github-issue-comment-cli from that\nsame untrusted checkout while the App token minted for\ntonic-ui-previews is live in the environment. A PR could modify those\nscripts to exfiltrate the token.\n\nCheck out the preview tooling separately from github.sha (the ref the\nworkflow was dispatched from, which requires write access to choose)\ninto ci-trusted-tooling/, and run it from there instead. Only the\npackage sources being previewed still come from the PR''s own checkout.\n\nThe comment step''s use of github.token is left as-is here -- unlike\nagentic-ui and tonic-one, this repo''s default workflow token\npermission hasn''t been confirmed to be the read-only ceiling that\nforces an App-token swap there.\n\n* fix(ci): close TOCTOU and token-exposure gaps in trusted tooling checkout\n\nSame two gaps found by Copilot review on the equivalent agentic-ui fix:\n\n1. The trusted-tooling checkout ran before Install packages / Build\n   public packages, both of which execute arbitrary PR-controlled\n   code. Since the checkout landed as a plain subdirectory of\n   $GITHUB_WORKSPACE, a malicious PR''s postinstall hook could\n   overwrite the \"trusted\" scripts before they were used. Move the\n   checkout to after both build steps.\n\n2. GH_TOKEN was exported for the whole comment step, including the\n   yarn add call against the PR''s own untrusted root package.json/\n   yarn.lock, which can run lifecycle scripts capable of reading the\n   token. Scope GH_TOKEN to only the final npx invocation, and disable\n   install scripts for the yarn add itself as defense in depth. This\n   applies even though the token here is still github.token, not an\n   App token -- the exposure principle is the same regardless of\n   which credential is live in the step.","tree":{"sha":"3d66b9940cc60a267e8c9e81f09ca9606a2269d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/3d66b9940cc60a267e8c9e81f09ca9606a2269d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/79e59835bb1718291fceb6eba6a490baa49015d2","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d66b9940cc60a267e8c9e81f09ca9606a2269d4\nparent f23b5922625e1fb4862a387b196001f9bf141bb2\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1785502779 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785502779 +0800\n\nfix(ci): source pr-preview tooling scripts from a trusted ref (#1186)\n\n* fix(ci): source pr-preview tooling scripts from a trusted ref\n\nThe job checks out the PR''s own head ref, then later steps run\nscripts/pr-preview/*.sh and scripts/github-issue-comment-cli from that\nsame untrusted checkout while the App token minted for\ntonic-ui-previews is live in the environment. A PR could modify those\nscripts to exfiltrate the token.\n\nCheck out the preview tooling separately from github.sha (the ref the\nworkflow was dispatched from, which requires write access to choose)\ninto ci-trusted-tooling/, and run it from there instead. Only the\npackage sources being previewed still come from the PR''s own checkout.\n\nThe comment step''s use of github.token is left as-is here -- unlike\nagentic-ui and tonic-one, this repo''s default workflow token\npermission hasn''t been confirmed to be the read-only ceiling that\nforces an App-token swap there.\n\n* fix(ci): close TOCTOU and token-exposure gaps in trusted tooling checkout\n\nSame two gaps found by Copilot review on the equivalent agentic-ui fix:\n\n1. The trusted-tooling checkout ran before Install packages / Build\n   public packages, both of which execute arbitrary PR-controlled\n   code. Since the checkout landed as a plain subdirectory of\n   $GITHUB_WORKSPACE, a malicious PR''s postinstall hook could\n   overwrite the \"trusted\" scripts before they were used. Move the\n   checkout to after both build steps.\n\n2. GH_TOKEN was exported for the whole comment step, including the\n   yarn add call against the PR''s own untrusted root package.json/\n   yarn.lock, which can run lifecycle scripts capable of reading the\n   token. Scope GH_TOKEN to only the final npx invocation, and disable\n   install scripts for the yarn add itself as defense in depth. This\n   applies even though the token here is still github.token, not an\n   App token -- the exposure principle is the same regardless of\n   which credential is live in the step.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcB