//api.github.com/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/0f7c3ce9c5e8c096df80883592209d33a067c1b3","node_id":"C_kwDODfyux9oAKDBmN2MzY2U5YzVlOGMwOTZkZjgwODgzNTkyMjA5ZDMzYTA2N2MxYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/1c1c1092d4d60db97f5b25ec80ca80eadc856ac7","sha":"1c1c1092d4d60db97f5b25ec80ca80eadc856ac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/1c1c1092d4d60db97f5b25ec80ca80eadc856ac7"}],"sha":"0f7c3ce9c5e8c096df80883592209d33a067c1b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/0f7c3ce9c5e8c096df80883592209d33a067c1b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/447801?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/1c1c1092d4d60db97f5b25ec80ca80eadc856ac7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T04:20:40Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T04:20:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: prepare v3 prerelease (#1168)\n\n* feat(react-docs): add micro-frontend examples (wujie + module-federation)\n\nPort the micro-frontend demo infrastructure: wujie host + sub-apps and\nmodule-federation shell + remotes (widget-os, widget-updates, inventory),\nshared inventory API, and the getting-started/micro-frontend page. widget-os\nrenders its chart via echarts directly. Adds build:mfe/dev:mfe scripts and the\nwujie-react / @module-federation/vite / vite / echarts dev deps; gitignores the\ngenerated public/mfe output.\n\n* feat(utils): add resolveTheme and toCSSVariable token-resolution helpers\n\nPorts the styled-system token-resolution engine from Tonic One: resolveTheme()\nresolves {token} references and attaches toColorMode(colorMode) (which exposes a\nget(path, default) helper), and toCSSVariable() maps a dotted/colon token path to\na CSS custom-property name. Exported from the @tonic-ui/utils barrel.\n\n* feat(react/theme): resolve theme via resolveTheme; useTheme exposes toColorMode().get()\n\ncreateTheme() now runs the merged theme through resolveTheme(), attaching\ntoColorMode(colorMode) (which carries a get(path, default) helper) and the\nTONIC_THEME sentinel; existing cssVariables behavior is preserved. useTheme()\nreturns theme.toColorMode(colorMode) (colorMode from ColorModeContext), so\ntheme.get(...) is available to consumers. Backward-compatible over flat v3\ntokens (no snapshot churn).\n\n* feat: align CSS-variables API to the new engine (useCSSVariables + __colorMode)\n\nstyled-system getter gates CSS-var emission on theme.useCSSVariables and resolves\n_dark/_light/main/value token shapes via props.__colorMode (dormant over flat v3);\na legacy colon->hyphen path preserves existing cssVariables behavior byte-for-byte.\nreact-base Box injects __colorMode from ColorModeContext (stripped from the DOM).\nTonicProvider/ThemeProvider thread a useCSSVariables prop into the theme; CSSVariables\nemits [data-color-scheme] blocks only when _dark/_light variants exist (none over flat\nv3). DarkMode/LightMode/InvertedMode set data-color-scheme. Default (useCSSVariables off)\nbehavior is unchanged: zero component snapshot churn.\n\n* fix(react-docs/mfe): use v3 scrollbar tokens in MFE GlobalStyles\n\nThe MFE host/shell GlobalStyles referenced v4-only colors._component.scrollbar.*\ntokens that don''t exist in the v3 theme (theme.get returned undefined). Switch to\nv3 colon tokens (gray:70/gray:30 track, white/black:disabled+tertiary thumb),\nmatching the docs site''s own GlobalStyles. Both demos now render with no console\nerrors (verified in-browser).\n\n* feat: generate TypeScript .d.ts for all packages (tsc --allowJs + rollup-plugin-dts)\n\nIntroduces the JSDoc-driven .d.ts generation pipeline from Tonic One across all 7\npackages (utils, styled-system, theme, react-base, react-hooks, react-icons, react):\na root tsconfig.base.json (allowJs, checkJs:false, emitDeclarationOnly), a per-package\ntsconfig + typed src/index.ts barrel, a rollup dts() output bundling to dist/index.d.ts\nwith injected global types (ForwardRefComponent/StyleProps/ThemeScales), and package.json\n\"types\" + types:build/types:clear wiring (typescript + rollup-plugin-dts devDeps).\ntypes:build pre-cleans @types/ so builds are idempotent. Pipeline-only: types are loose\n(inferred) except react-base''s Box; per-component JSDoc annotation is deferred.\n\n* docs(react-docs): document theme.get and the useCSSVariables API\n\nAlign the theming docs to the new engine for what v3 actually supports: theme.get\n(via useTheme/toColorMode) on the usage + useColorStyle pages, and the useCSSVariables\nprop emitting --tonic-* CSS variables over flat v3 tokens on the usage + css-theme-variables\npages. Color mode/style remain driven by colorStyle; semantic _dark/_light token switching\nis intentionally not documented (deferred with the v4 semantic tokens).\n\n* fix: dedupe imports + sync CSSVariables export test (integration fixups)\n\nMerge the duplicate @tonic-ui/utils import in styled-system getter.js and the\nduplicate ../theme import in TonicProvider.js (import/no-duplicates lint errors\nintroduced while aligning the CSS-variables API), and add CSSVariables to the\nreact package''s expected-exports test (it is now part of the public @tonic-ui/react\nsurface). Full sweep green: 756 tests, 0 lint errors, all builds + dts + docs.\n\n* feat: add tonic-ui-version.config.js for centralized doc version management\n\nSingle version registry (v3 prerelease on main, v2 current, v1) driving the docs\nversion switcher, versions page, per-version env vars, and ci-branch''s version\nlabel. ci-branch resolves the current(:true) entry (v2, base path unchanged);\ntonic-ui.env generates per-version vars via a config-driven loop (drops v0);\nnext.config bakes literal env (labels, base URL, prerelease labels); Header builds\nthe switcher from those literals (no dynamic process.env keys, so URLs inline into\nthe bundle); versions page gains v3 + Preview badge. Mirrors tonic-one PR #402.\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for high-traffic primitives (U14-E1)\n\nPort @typedef + @type {ForwardRefComponent<...>} JSDoc from tonic-one for\nbutton, text, flex, grid, stack, link, icon. Adds ''import React'' where the\nJSDoc references React.* (required by tsc; yields no-unused-vars *warnings*\neslint cannot resolve from JSDoc comments).\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest E1 dirs 54/54, 8 snapshots, zero\nchurn; lint 0 errors. Variant/size unions adapted to tonic-ui v3 values.\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for form controls (U14-E2)\n\nPort @typedef + @type {ForwardRefComponent<...>} JSDoc from tonic-one for\ninput, textarea, checkbox, radio, switch, select, search-input,\nform-control, autocomplete (35 files). Variant/size unions adapted to\ntonic-ui v3 (e.g. Select = outline|filled|unstyled; Input keeps flush).\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest E2 dirs 14 suites/166 tests/9\nsnapshots zero churn; lint 0 errors (React no-unused-vars warnings only).\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for overlays/feedback (U14-E3)\n\nPort @typedef + @type {ForwardRefComponent<...>}/{StyledFC<...>} JSDoc from\ntonic-one for modal, drawer, popover, popper, portal, tooltip, toast, alert,\nspinner, progress, skeleton, badge, tag (48 files). Props adapted to v3.\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; lint 0 errors (React no-unused-vars\nwarnings only); jest 10 snapshots zero churn. The one batch test failure\n(tooltip closeOnClick) is pre-existing popper/transition timing flakiness\n(passes 3/3 in isolation; diff is comment-only), not a regression.\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for navigation/structure (U14-E4)\n\nPort @typedef + @type {ForwardRefComponent<...>} JSDoc from tonic-one for\naccordion, tabs, menu, table, tree, pagination, truncate, image,\nvisually-hidden (46 files; list already done, breadcrumb absent). Props\nadapted to v3.\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest 15 suites/90 tests/8 snapshots\nzero churn (menu/Submenu green this run); lint 0 errors (React no-unused-vars\nwarnings + 1 pre-existing unused-disable in a test file).\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for misc components (U14-E5a)\n\nPort @typedef + @type JSDoc from tonic-one for button-box, code, divider,\nhighlight, mark, space, resize-handle, scrollbar (6), animate-presence, and\ndeprecated components (accordion-collapse, calendar, submenu-toggle, table\nheader cell/row) — 19 files. Props adapted to v3.\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest 15 suites/150 tests/9 snapshots\nzero churn; lint 0 errors (React no-unused-vars warnings only).\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for engine-touched + date/transition components (U14-E5b)\n\nPort @typedef + @type JSDoc from tonic-one for color-mode (4), provider/\nTonicProvider, theme/createTheme, transitions (6), date-pickers (9) = 21 files.\n\ncreateTheme JSDoc ADAPTED to tonic-ui''s engine signature (cssVariables:\nboolean|CSSVariableConfig default false; optional cssVariablePrefix/\ncssVariables/rootSelector return), not tonic-one''s. Engine logic untouched\n(diffs are comment/import-only).\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest 15 suites/72 tests/1 snapshot zero\nchurn (date-pickers green this run); lint 0 errors (React warnings only).\n\n* chore: add loop-engineering state and refine doc version config\n\nLoop spine for the styled-system engine migration + U14 JSDoc annotation work:\n- .states/migrate-styled-system-to-tonic-ui/ STATE.md (spine), whitelist\n  .gitignore, and planning docs (token-mapping, port-plan, jsdoc-dts-plan,\n  version-config-plan).\n\nDoc version-config refinements:\n- react-docs/next.config.mjs, versions/index.page.mdx.template,\n  scripts/update-tonic-ui-vars.mjs, tonic-ui.env\n- tonic-ui-version.config.js\n\n* chore: add loop-engineering state for styled-system migration + U14\n\nLoop spine tracking the styled-system engine migration and U14 JSDoc\nannotation work:\n- STATE.md (the resumable spine)\n- whitelist .gitignore (commits only spine + docs, ignores scratch)\n- docs/: token-mapping, port-plan, jsdoc-dts-plan, version-config-plan\n\n* refactor(react-docs): clarify tonic-ui.env version-config loader\n\nUse '':'' delimiter, add explanatory comments, readonly CONFIG_PATH, and a\nclearer TONIC_UI_VERSION_PREFIX variable name.\n\n* chore(loop): record Phase 2 PR + Phase 3/4 backlog\n\n- U12 Phase 2 PR #1168 opened (draft, feat/semantic-token-css-variables -> main).\n- Add Phase 3 (clone v4 theme tokens, match v4 docs, getting-started + migration\n  guide updates for new primitive/semantic tokens) with V1-V7 units + gating Qs.\n- Add Phase 4 (migrate all components to semantic tokens) with W1-Wn units.\n\n* build: align package build/types mechanism with tonic-one (U18)\n\nUnify all six published packages (utils, styled-system, react-base,\nreact-hooks, theme, react) onto tonic-one''s single-source build pipeline:\n\n- single `src/index.ts` entry per package (delete the parallel runtime\n  `src/index.js`; the `.ts` barrel already mirrored its exports)\n- babel `@babel/preset-typescript` ({ rewriteImportExtensions: true })\n  compiles the .ts entry for the CJS/ESM builds\n- rollup: one `input` drives all three outputs (cjs, esm, dist/index.d.ts);\n  babel plugin gets configFile + exclude + extensions, nodeResolve gets\n  extensions; codecov plugin retained in cjs/esm\n- dts via rollup-plugin-dts reading JSDoc directly (allowJs) — drop the\n  separate `tsc`/`types:build`/`@types` step (build = rollup only),\n  removing the prior idempotency hazard\n- injectGlobalTypes() kept where global.d.ts exists (react-base, react);\n  theme cjs keeps exports:''named''\n- tsconfig.json simplified to the minimal extends-base shape\n\nVerified: `yarn build-public` idempotent (2x), every public package emits\na real dist/index.d.ts (react 6612 lines, unchanged; codemod stays JS-only),\nreact suite 756/756 green with zero snapshot churn, lint clean.\n\n* chore(loop): record U18 build/types mechanism alignment (done, committed d066e056ec)\n\n* chore(react): remove legacy .eslintrc.js (flat eslint.config.mjs is authoritative post-upgrade)\n\n* chore(react): align eslint config with tonic-one (@typescript-eslint parser)\n\nSwitch the react package''s flat eslint config to @typescript-eslint/parser +\ntsPlugin recommended/stylistic (mirroring tonic-one), so JSDoc type\nreferences like `React.ReactNode` count as using the `React` import. This\nremoves the spurious `''React'' is defined but never used` no-unused-vars\nwarnings without editing the 146 source files (keeping them byte-identical\nto tonic-one for frictionless future ports).\n\n- parser: @babel/eslint-parser -> @typescript-eslint/parser\n- keep @typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars ON ([''warn'', ignore ^_]) so genuine\n  dead code is still flagged (verified via probe); base no-unused-vars off\n- ignore generated dirs (@types from the old pre-U18 tsc step, global.d.ts);\n  removed the orphaned stale @types/ output\n- devDeps: @typescript-eslint/{parser,eslint-plugin} ^8.58.0\n- lint script --ext now includes .ts,.tsx\n\nreact lint: 0 errors, 0 React-import warnings (was 125 warnings; 96 remain,\nall legitimate unused-arg / jsx-no-bind / etc.).\n\n* chore(loop): record U19 eslint config alignment (done, e45f67081a)\n\n* feat: theme package parity\n\n* feat: utils package parity\n\n* feat: styled-system parity\n\n* feat: react-base parity\n\n* feat: react-docs and mcp parity\n\n- Align eslint configs across changelog-github, codemod, mcp, react-base, react-docs\n- Add ColorPaletteV3, ColorPreview, ThemeTokens components; remove ThemeParser\n- Add FigmaIcon; update all react-docs components for semantic token CSS variables\n- Update mcp rollup config and server tests\n- Update react-docs pages for new token/theme system\n\n* fix: fix yarn test errors after exports update\n\n* fix: set IS_REACT_ACT_ENVIRONMENT for React 18 act() compatibility in jsdom\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: update test snapshots\n\n* chore: upgrade @testing-library/react to v16 and wrap state updates in act()\n\n- Upgrade @testing-library/react from ^15 to ^16 and @testing-library/user-event from ^14.4.3 to ^14.0.0 across react, react-base, react-hooks packages\n- Add @testing-library/dom ^10.0.0 as explicit peer dependency in react package\n- Remove IS_REACT_ACT_ENVIRONMENT global from react-base, react-docs, and react-hooks jest-setup (v16 handles this internally)\n- Wrap direct DOM event dispatches and focus() calls in act() to suppress React 18+ warnings in tests\n\n* test(menu): stabilize submenu portal click test against CI flakiness\n\nSet closeOnSelect={false} on the Menu in the portal click-event tests so\nthe post-click ''menu still open'' assertion no longer races the menu-list\nexit transition. With the default (true), clicking a submenu item calls\nthe parent menu''s onClose, starting the Collapse exit transition followed\nby unmountOnExit; the assertion passed on fast machines that read it\nmid-transition and failed on slower CI that read it after unmount.\n\n* refactor(theme): rename v3 primitiveTheme/semanticTheme locals to *Tokens\n\nThe token-factory functions return token collections, not full themes;\nonly the merged createTheme result is the theme. Rename the local\nvariables to match. deprecatedTheme (a real v2 theme) is left as-is.\n\n* chore(theme): remove redundant file-path header comments in v3\n\nThe leading `// primitives/...` and `// semantic/...` path comments\nrestate the file''s own location and add no information. Drop them.\n\n* refactor(theme): align docs with v3 token structure\n\n- Export createPrimitiveTokens/createSemanticTokens as named exports in v3 (drop default exports)\n- Migrate ThemeTokens docs component to @tanstack/react-table and v3 primitive / v2 legacy token paths\n- Update sizes/space doc pages to v3 primitive paths and PageHeader to semantic text color tokens\n\n* chore: remove trailing blank lines in jest-setup files\n\nFixes @stylistic/no-multiple-empty-lines lint errors.\n\n* ci: switch workflow triggers from v2 to main branch\n\nUpdate push/pull_request branch triggers across all workflows and point\nAlgolia indexing at the tonic-ui-v3 index. Also remove the now-stale\ncomment block in ci-branch about the hardcoded [v2] trigger.\n\n* chore: relax cross-env version range and add missing dependency to codemod\n\n* feat(box): add internal __sx prop for lowest-priority base styles\n\nLets components apply base styles via __sx that consumer style props\nand sx can still override, without forwarding __sx to the DOM.\n\n* docs: add ADR, spec, and plan docs for sx base channel and mfe architecture\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(skills): rename tonic-ui-slot-migration to tonic-ui-slots\n\nRestructures the slot migration skill under the standard SKILL.md convention.\n\n* docs(sx): add tonic-ui-sx skill, ADR, and internals migration plan\n\n- Add tonic-ui-sx skill covering the sx vs __sx channel decision and mergeSx fold, with evals\n- Add ADR for routing transition-component animation state through __sx in both render modes\n- Add implementation plan for migrating internal __sx usage across react and react-data-grid\n- Document Scrollbar''s scrollView slot in the tonic-ui-slots skill\n- Fix stale \"Tonic One\" naming in tonic-ui-pr skill and mfe-architecture-design plan\n\n* fix(utils): prevent ReDoS in resolveTheme token-matching regex\n\nRestrict the inline token-reference regex to exclude braces in its\ncharacter class, avoiding catastrophic backtracking on malformed\ninput with long runs of unclosed braces (flagged by CodeQL).\n\n* chore: update SKILL.md\n\n* fix(mcp): read actual bound port in CLI HTTP transport tests\n\nThe streamable-http/sse tests hardcoded port 3000 for both the startup\nlog match and the follow-up request, but the CLI''s findAvailablePort\nfalls back to a different port whenever 3000 is already taken (e.g. by\na locally running docs dev server), causing the tests to time out.\n\n* docs: fix incorrect theme imports and routes\n\n* fix(sx): compose nested selectors per-declaration in array merge\n\nArray items in sx() were merged with a shallow spread, so a later item\ntouching the same nested selector (e.g. &:hover) silently discarded every\ndeclaration an earlier item made there instead of overriding just the\nredeclared properties.\n\n* feat: update Claude skills\n\n* feat: add internal `composeSx` utility\n\n* chore: update github repo\n\n* feat: add codesandbox button back\n\n* chore: bump all React package versions to \"^18.3.0 || ^19.0.0\"\n\n* Create changeset for v3 prerelease\n\nAdded a changeset for the v3 prerelease preparation.\n\n* chore: align react-docs sandbox with v3 CSS variables setup\n\nBump CodeSandbox dependency versions to 3.x and add @emotion/styled.\nUpdate the CRA template to match the getting-started guide: enable\nCSS variables via TonicProvider''s useCSSVariables instead of the\ndeprecated createTheme({ cssVariables: true }), drop colorStyle in\nfavor of semantic tokens, and sync scrollbar/global styles with\ntheme.get().\n\n* chore(loop): v0->v1 schema migration for migrate-styled-system-to-tonic-ui\n\nStamp Schema: v1, remove the legacy .gitignore whitelist (it hid\nnothing), and re-queue the stale U20 claim (no matching commit found).\n\n* chore(loop): claim U20, narrow scope after verification\n\nCross-checked every package''s eslint.config.mjs against tonic-one.\nMost already match modulo the two approved uniform deltas; the real\nremaining gaps are mcp (missing no-trailing-spaces rule, downgraded\nno-unused-vars) and react-hooks (extra rules + test-file override\nnot present upstream).\n\n* chore(react-hooks,mcp): align eslint configs with tonic-one (U20)\n\nAdd mcp''s missing no-trailing-spaces rule and revert its\nno-unused-vars to tonic-one''s exact form. In react-hooks, drop two\nnon-load-bearing deviations and keep two load-bearing ones with\nfile:line-cited comments (prefer-for-of off for useClickOutside.js;\nthe test-file override for useCopyToClipboard.test.js/useId.test.js).\n\nAlso clean up the loop''s state file: mark U20 done, and remove stale\nduplicate entries in ## Next (U3-U15/U12-PR block and the U14\nsub-unit-E list) that were already completed under different unit\nlabels with matching commits.\n\n* chore(loop): archive migrate-styled-system-to-tonic-ui (Phase 2 complete)\n\nHeader + ## Done + full ## Log copied to .states/_archive/ so the\ncompleted loop stays visible/minable after .states/<name>/ is\nremoved. Phase 3/4 (provisional, gated on PR #1168 merging to main)\nnever started under this loop and are intentionally not archived\nhere per protocol — flagged in the archive''s closing note.\n\n* chore(loop): extract Phase 3/4 provisional plan before dir removal\n\nFull context (open questions, resolutions, provisional V1-V7/W1-Wfinal\nunit lists) for the parked v4-theme-token phases, preserved outside\nthe loop directory being deleted next.\n\n* chore(loop): remove migrate-styled-system-to-tonic-ui loop directory\n\nPhase 2 is complete (archived in .states/_archive/); Phase 3/4\nprovisional plan preserved there too. Final act of the completion\nprotocol.\n\n* fix(loop): archive the full final STATE.md, not extracted sections\n\nPer loop-engineering v1.2, the archive should preserve the whole\noriginal final state file, not just header+Done+Log. Replaces the\nextracted archive with the exact STATE.md content from immediately\nbefore the loop directory was removed.\n\n* fix(loop): restore the loop''s docs/ into the archive too\n\nThe docs/ directory (token-mapping.md, port-plan.md, jsdoc-dts-plan.md,\nversion-config-plan.md) was deleted along with STATE.md but never\narchived, leaving the archived STATE.md''s own ## Docs section\npointing at nothing. Restored all 4 files byte-for-byte from history.\n\n* chore(loop): trim archived docs to the one with forward-looking value\n\nDrop port-plan.md, jsdoc-dts-plan.md, version-config-plan.md from the\narchive -- execution plans for now-fully-shipped Phase 2 units with no\nforward dependency (the archived STATE.md''s Done/Log already records\nwhat happened, with commit refs). Move token-mapping.md -- the one\ndoc Phase 3 (v4 semantic tokens) will actually need -- to the repo''s\ntop-level docs/plans/ instead of nesting it under the loop archive,\nand repoint the archived STATE.md''s ## Docs entry accordingly.\n\n* chore(loop): drop ## Docs entry for token-mapping.md\n\nA new skill will own token mapping going forward, so the archived\nloop''s state no longer needs to reference it. The doc itself stays\nat docs/plans/2026-06-26-token-mapping.md for that skill to build on.\n\n* chore(loop): drop archived note and redundant phase3-4 extract\n\nThe full STATE.md already carries Phase 3/4''s provisional plan in\n## Next, making the standalone phase3-4-provisional-plan.md\nredundant. The archived note was bookkeeping about the archival\nprocess itself, not loop content worth keeping.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2def473dd57ce50b6733a21e2188755159c6ebbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/2def473dd57ce50b6733a21e2188755159c6ebbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/1c1c1092d4d60db97f5b25ec80ca80eadc856ac7","verification":{"payload":"tree 2def473dd57ce50b6733a21e2188755159c6ebbc\nparent 464e358d7b4c439c4c2cf9a9b4853c2603a1a5cb\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1784348440 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784348440 +0800\n\nfeat: prepare v3 prerelease (#1168)\n\n* feat(react-docs): add micro-frontend examples (wujie + module-federation)\n\nPort the micro-frontend demo infrastructure: wujie host + sub-apps and\nmodule-federation shell + remotes (widget-os, widget-updates, inventory),\nshared inventory API, and the getting-started/micro-frontend page. widget-os\nrenders its chart via echarts directly. Adds build:mfe/dev:mfe scripts and the\nwujie-react / @module-federation/vite / vite / echarts dev deps; gitignores the\ngenerated public/mfe output.\n\n* feat(utils): add resolveTheme and toCSSVariable token-resolution helpers\n\nPorts the styled-system token-resolution engine from Tonic One: resolveTheme()\nresolves {token} references and attaches toColorMode(colorMode) (which exposes a\nget(path, default) helper), and toCSSVariable() maps a dotted/colon token path to\na CSS custom-property name. Exported from the @tonic-ui/utils barrel.\n\n* feat(react/theme): resolve theme via resolveTheme; useTheme exposes toColorMode().get()\n\ncreateTheme() now runs the merged theme through resolveTheme(), attaching\ntoColorMode(colorMode) (which carries a get(path, default) helper) and the\nTONIC_THEME sentinel; existing cssVariables behavior is preserved. useTheme()\nreturns theme.toColorMode(colorMode) (colorMode from ColorModeContext), so\ntheme.get(...) is available to consumers. Backward-compatible over flat v3\ntokens (no snapshot churn).\n\n* feat: align CSS-variables API to the new engine (useCSSVariables + __colorMode)\n\nstyled-system getter gates CSS-var emission on theme.useCSSVariables and resolves\n_dark/_light/main/value token shapes via props.__colorMode (dormant over flat v3);\na legacy colon->hyphen path preserves existing cssVariables behavior byte-for-byte.\nreact-base Box injects __colorMode from ColorModeContext (stripped from the DOM).\nTonicProvider/ThemeProvider thread a useCSSVariables prop into the theme; CSSVariables\nemits [data-color-scheme] blocks only when _dark/_light variants exist (none over flat\nv3). DarkMode/LightMode/InvertedMode set data-color-scheme. Default (useCSSVariables off)\nbehavior is unchanged: zero component snapshot churn.\n\n* fix(react-docs/mfe): use v3 scrollbar tokens in MFE GlobalStyles\n\nThe MFE host/shell GlobalStyles referenced v4-only colors._component.scrollbar.*\ntokens that don''t exist in the v3 theme (theme.get returned undefined). Switch to\nv3 colon tokens (gray:70/gray:30 track, white/black:disabled+tertiary thumb),\nmatching the docs site''s own GlobalStyles. Both demos now render with no console\nerrors (verified in-browser).\n\n* feat: generate TypeScript .d.ts for all packages (tsc --allowJs + rollup-plugin-dts)\n\nIntroduces the JSDoc-driven .d.ts generation pipeline from Tonic One across all 7\npackages (utils, styled-system, theme, react-base, react-hooks, react-icons, react):\na root tsconfig.base.json (allowJs, checkJs:false, emitDeclarationOnly), a per-package\ntsconfig + typed src/index.ts barrel, a rollup dts() output bundling to dist/index.d.ts\nwith injected global types (ForwardRefComponent/StyleProps/ThemeScales), and package.json\n\"types\" + types:build/types:clear wiring (typescript + rollup-plugin-dts devDeps).\ntypes:build pre-cleans @types/ so builds are idempotent. Pipeline-only: types are loose\n(inferred) except react-base''s Box; per-component JSDoc annotation is deferred.\n\n* docs(react-docs): document theme.get and the useCSSVariables API\n\nAlign the theming docs to the new engine for what v3 actually supports: theme.get\n(via useTheme/toColorMode) on the usage + useColorStyle pages, and the useCSSVariables\nprop emitting --tonic-* CSS variables over flat v3 tokens on the usage + css-theme-variables\npages. Color mode/style remain driven by colorStyle; semantic _dark/_light token switching\nis intentionally not documented (deferred with the v4 semantic tokens).\n\n* fix: dedupe imports + sync CSSVariables export test (integration fixups)\n\nMerge the duplicate @tonic-ui/utils import in styled-system getter.js and the\nduplicate ../theme import in TonicProvider.js (import/no-duplicates lint errors\nintroduced while aligning the CSS-variables API), and add CSSVariables to the\nreact package''s expected-exports test (it is now part of the public @tonic-ui/react\nsurface). Full sweep green: 756 tests, 0 lint errors, all builds + dts + docs.\n\n* feat: add tonic-ui-version.config.js for centralized doc version management\n\nSingle version registry (v3 prerelease on main, v2 current, v1) driving the docs\nversion switcher, versions page, per-version env vars, and ci-branch''s version\nlabel. ci-branch resolves the current(:true) entry (v2, base path unchanged);\ntonic-ui.env generates per-version vars via a config-driven loop (drops v0);\nnext.config bakes literal env (labels, base URL, prerelease labels); Header builds\nthe switcher from those literals (no dynamic process.env keys, so URLs inline into\nthe bundle); versions page gains v3 + Preview badge. Mirrors tonic-one PR #402.\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for high-traffic primitives (U14-E1)\n\nPort @typedef + @type {ForwardRefComponent<...>} JSDoc from tonic-one for\nbutton, text, flex, grid, stack, link, icon. Adds ''import React'' where the\nJSDoc references React.* (required by tsc; yields no-unused-vars *warnings*\neslint cannot resolve from JSDoc comments).\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest E1 dirs 54/54, 8 snapshots, zero\nchurn; lint 0 errors. Variant/size unions adapted to tonic-ui v3 values.\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for form controls (U14-E2)\n\nPort @typedef + @type {ForwardRefComponent<...>} JSDoc from tonic-one for\ninput, textarea, checkbox, radio, switch, select, search-input,\nform-control, autocomplete (35 files). Variant/size unions adapted to\ntonic-ui v3 (e.g. Select = outline|filled|unstyled; Input keeps flush).\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest E2 dirs 14 suites/166 tests/9\nsnapshots zero churn; lint 0 errors (React no-unused-vars warnings only).\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for overlays/feedback (U14-E3)\n\nPort @typedef + @type {ForwardRefComponent<...>}/{StyledFC<...>} JSDoc from\ntonic-one for modal, drawer, popover, popper, portal, tooltip, toast, alert,\nspinner, progress, skeleton, badge, tag (48 files). Props adapted to v3.\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; lint 0 errors (React no-unused-vars\nwarnings only); jest 10 snapshots zero churn. The one batch test failure\n(tooltip closeOnClick) is pre-existing popper/transition timing flakiness\n(passes 3/3 in isolation; diff is comment-only), not a regression.\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for navigation/structure (U14-E4)\n\nPort @typedef + @type {ForwardRefComponent<...>} JSDoc from tonic-one for\naccordion, tabs, menu, table, tree, pagination, truncate, image,\nvisually-hidden (46 files; list already done, breadcrumb absent). Props\nadapted to v3.\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest 15 suites/90 tests/8 snapshots\nzero churn (menu/Submenu green this run); lint 0 errors (React no-unused-vars\nwarnings + 1 pre-existing unused-disable in a test file).\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for misc components (U14-E5a)\n\nPort @typedef + @type JSDoc from tonic-one for button-box, code, divider,\nhighlight, mark, space, resize-handle, scrollbar (6), animate-presence, and\ndeprecated components (accordion-collapse, calendar, submenu-toggle, table\nheader cell/row) — 19 files. Props adapted to v3.\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest 15 suites/150 tests/9 snapshots\nzero churn; lint 0 errors (React no-unused-vars warnings only).\n\n* feat(react): add JSDoc type annotations for engine-touched + date/transition components (U14-E5b)\n\nPort @typedef + @type JSDoc from tonic-one for color-mode (4), provider/\nTonicProvider, theme/createTheme, transitions (6), date-pickers (9) = 21 files.\n\ncreateTheme JSDoc ADAPTED to tonic-ui''s engine signature (cssVariables:\nboolean|CSSVariableConfig default false; optional cssVariablePrefix/\ncssVariables/rootSelector return), not tonic-one''s. Engine logic untouched\n(diffs are comment/import-only).\n\nVerified: types:build (tsc) exit 0; jest 15 suites/72 tests/1 snapshot zero\nchurn (date-pickers green this run); lint 0 errors (React warnings only).\n\n* chore: add loop-engineering state and refine doc version config\n\nLoop spine for the styled-system engine migration + U14 JSDoc annotation work:\n- .states/migrate-styled-system-to-tonic-ui/ STATE.md (spine), whitelist\n  .gitignore, and planning docs (token-mapping, port-plan, jsdoc-dts-plan,\n  version-config-plan).\n\nDoc version-config refinements:\n- react-docs/next.config.mjs, versions/index.page.mdx.template,\n  scripts/update-tonic-ui-vars.mjs, tonic-ui.env\n- tonic-ui-version.config.js\n\n* chore: add loop-engineering state for styled-system migration + U14\n\nLoop spine tracking the styled-system engine migration and U14 JSDoc\nannotation work:\n- STATE.md (the resumable spine)\n- whitelist .gitignore (commits only spine + docs, ignores scratch)\n- docs/: token-mapping, port-plan, jsdoc-dts-plan, version-config-plan\n\n* refactor(react-docs): clarify tonic-ui.env version-config loader\n\nUse '':'' delimiter, add explanatory comments, readonly CONFIG_PATH, and a\nclearer TONIC_UI_VERSION_PREFIX variable name.\n\n* chore(loop): record Phase 2 PR + Phase 3/4 backlog\n\n- U12 Phase 2 PR #1168 opened (draft, feat/semantic-token-css-variables -> main).\n- Add Phase 3 (clone v4 theme tokens, match v4 docs, getting-started + migration\n  guide updates for new primitive/semantic tokens) with V1-V7 units + gating Qs.\n- Add Phase 4 (migrate all components to semantic tokens) with W1-Wn units.\n\n* build: align package build/types mechanism with tonic-one (U18)\n\nUnify all six published packages (utils, styled-system, react-base,\nreact-hooks, theme, react) onto tonic-one''s single-source build pipeline:\n\n- single `src/index.ts` entry per package (delete the parallel runtime\n  `src/index.js`; the `.ts` barrel already mirrored its exports)\n- babel `@babel/preset-typescript` ({ rewriteImportExtensions: true })\n  compiles the .ts entry for the CJS/ESM builds\n- rollup: one `input` drives all three outputs (cjs, esm, dist/index.d.ts);\n  babel plugin gets configFile + exclude + extensions, nodeResolve gets\n  extensions; codecov plugin retained in cjs/esm\n- dts via rollup-plugin-dts reading JSDoc directly (allowJs) — drop the\n  separate `tsc`/`types:build`/`@types` step (build = rollup only),\n  removing the prior idempotency hazard\n- injectGlobalTypes() kept where global.d.ts exists (react-base, react);\n  theme cjs keeps exports:''named''\n- tsconfig.json simplified to the minimal extends-base shape\n\nVerified: `yarn build-public` idempotent (2x), every public package emits\na real dist/index.d.ts (react 6612 lines, unchanged; codemod stays JS-only),\nreact suite 756/756 green with zero snapshot churn, lint clean.\n\n* chore(loop): record U18 build/types mechanism alignment (done, committed d066e056ec)\n\n* chore(react): remove legacy .eslintrc.js (flat eslint.config.mjs is authoritative post-upgrade)\n\n* chore(react): align eslint config with tonic-one (@typescript-eslint parser)\n\nSwitch the react package''s flat eslint config to @typescript-eslint/parser +\ntsPlugin recommended/stylistic (mirroring tonic-one), so JSDoc type\nreferences like `React.ReactNode` count as using the `React` import. This\nremoves the spurious `''React'' is defined but never used` no-unused-vars\nwarnings without editing the 146 source files (keeping them byte-identical\nto tonic-one for frictionless future ports).\n\n- parser: @babel/eslint-parser -> @typescript-eslint/parser\n- keep @typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars ON ([''warn'', ignore ^_]) so genuine\n  dead code is still flagged (verified via probe); base no-unused-vars off\n- ignore generated dirs (@types from the old pre-U18 tsc step, global.d.ts);\n  removed the orphaned stale @types/ output\n- devDeps: @typescript-eslint/{parser,eslint-plugin} ^8.58.0\n- lint script --ext now includes .ts,.tsx\n\nreact lint: 0 errors, 0 React-import warnings (was 125 warnings; 96 remain,\nall legitimate unused-arg / jsx-no-bind / etc.).\n\n* chore(loop): record U19 eslint config alignment (done, e45f67081a)\n\n* feat: theme package parity\n\n* feat: utils package parity\n\n* feat: styled-system parity\n\n* feat: react-base parity\n\n* feat: react-docs and mcp parity\n\n- Align eslint configs across changelog-github, codemod, mcp, react-base, react-docs\n- Add ColorPaletteV3, ColorPreview, ThemeTokens components; remove ThemeParser\n- Add FigmaIcon; update all react-docs components for semantic token CSS variables\n- Update mcp rollup config and server tests\n- Update react-docs pages for new token/theme system\n\n* fix: fix yarn test errors after exports update\n\n* fix: set IS_REACT_ACT_ENVIRONMENT for React 18 act() compatibility in jsdom\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: update test snapshots\n\n* chore: upgrade @testing-library/react to v16 and wrap state updates in act()\n\n- Upgrade @testing-library/react from ^15 to ^16 and @testing-library/user-event from ^14.4.3 to ^14.0.0 across react, react-base, react-hooks packages\n- Add @testing-library/dom ^10.0.0 as explicit peer dependency in react package\n- Remove IS_REACT_ACT_ENVIRONMENT global from react-base, react-docs, and react-hooks jest-setup (v16 handles this internally)\n- Wrap direct DOM event dispatches and focus() calls in act() to suppress React 18+ warnings in tests\n\n* test(menu): stabilize submenu portal click test against CI flakiness\n\nSet closeOnSelect={false} on the Menu in the portal click-event tests so\nthe post-click ''menu still open'' assertion no longer races the menu-list\nexit transition. With the default (true), clicking a submenu item calls\nthe parent menu''s onClose, starting the Collapse exit transition followed\nby unmountOnExit; the assertion passed on fast machines that read it\nmid-transition and failed on slower CI that read it after unmount.\n\n* refactor(theme): rename v3 primitiveTheme/semanticTheme locals to *Tokens\n\nThe token-factory functions return token collections, not full themes;\nonly the merged createTheme result is the theme. Rename the local\nvariables to match. deprecatedTheme (a real v2 theme) is left as-is.\n\n* chore(theme): remove redundant file-path header comments in v3\n\nThe leading `// primitives/...` and `// semantic/...` path comments\nrestate the file''s own location and add no information. Drop them.\n\n* refactor(theme): align docs with v3 token structure\n\n- Export createPrimitiveTokens/createSemanticTokens as named exports in v3 (drop default exports)\n- Migrate ThemeTokens docs component to @tanstack/react-table and v3 primitive / v2 legacy token paths\n- Update sizes/space doc pages to v3 primitive paths and PageHeader to semantic text color tokens\n\n* chore: remove trailing blank lines in jest-setup files\n\nFixes @stylistic/no-multiple-empty-lines lint errors.\n\n* ci: switch workflow triggers from v2 to main branch\n\nUpdate push/pull_request branch triggers across all workflows and point\nAlgolia indexing at the tonic-ui-v3 index. Also remove the now-stale\ncomment block in ci-branch about the hardcoded [v2] trigger.\n\n* chore: relax cross-env version range and add missing dependency to codemod\n\n* feat(box): add internal __sx prop for lowest-priority base styles\n\nLets components apply base styles via __sx that consumer style props\nand sx can still override, without forwarding __sx to the DOM.\n\n* docs: add ADR, spec, and plan docs for sx base channel and mfe architecture\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(skills): rename tonic-ui-slot-migration to tonic-ui-slots\n\nRestructures the slot migration skill under the standard SKILL.md convention.\n\n* docs(sx): add tonic-ui-sx skill, ADR, and internals migration plan\n\n- Add tonic-ui-sx skill covering the sx vs __sx channel decision and mergeSx fold, with evals\n- Add ADR for routing transition-component animation state through __sx in both render modes\n- Add implementation plan for migrating internal __sx usage across react and react-data-grid\n- Document Scrollbar''s scrollView slot in the tonic-ui-slots skill\n- Fix stale \"Tonic One\" naming in tonic-ui-pr skill and mfe-architecture-design plan\n\n* fix(utils): prevent ReDoS in resolveTheme token-matching regex\n\nRestrict the inline token-reference regex to exclude braces in its\ncharacter class, avoiding catastrophic backtracking on malformed\ninput with long runs of unclosed braces (flagged by CodeQL).\n\n* chore: update SKILL.md\n\n* fix(mcp): read actual bound port in CLI HTTP transport tests\n\nThe streamable-http/sse tests hardcoded port 3000 for both the startup\nlog match and the follow-up request, but the CLI''s findAvailablePort\nfalls back to a different port whenever 3000 is already taken (e.g. by\na locally running docs dev server), causing the tests to time out.\n\n* docs: fix incorrect theme imports and routes\n\n* fix(sx): compose nested selectors per-declaration in array merge\n\nArray items in sx() were merged with a shallow spread, so a later item\ntouching the same nested selector (e.g. &:hover) silently discarded every\ndeclaration an earlier item made there instead of overriding just the\nredeclared properties.\n\n* feat: update Claude skills\n\n* feat: add internal `composeSx` utility\n\n* chore: update github repo\n\n* feat: add codesandbox button back\n\n* chore: bump all React package versions to \"^18.3.0 || ^19.0.0\"\n\n* Create changeset for v3 prerelease\n\nAdded a changeset for the v3 prerelease preparation.\n\n* chore: align react-docs sandbox with v3 CSS variables setup\n\nBump CodeSandbox dependency versions to 3.x and add @emotion/styled.\nUpdate the CRA template to match the getting-started guide: enable\nCSS variables via TonicProvider''s useCSSVariables instead of the\ndeprecated createTheme({ cssVariables: true }), drop colorStyle in\nfavor of semantic tokens, and sync scrollbar/global styles with\ntheme.get().\n\n* chore(loop): v0->v1 schema migration for migrate-styled-system-to-tonic-ui\n\nStamp Schema: v1, remove the legacy .gitignore whitelist (it hid\nnothing), and re-queue the stale U20 claim (no matching commit found).\n\n* chore(loop): claim U20, narrow scope after verification\n\nCross-checked every package''s eslint.config.mjs against tonic-one.\nMost already match modulo the two approved uniform deltas; the real\nremaining gaps are mcp (missing no-trailing-spaces rule, downgraded\nno-unused-vars) and react-hooks (extra rules + test-file override\nnot present upstream).\n\n* chore(react-hooks,mcp): align eslint configs with tonic-one (U20)\n\nAdd mcp''s missing no-trailing-spaces rule and revert its\nno-unused-vars to tonic-one''s exact form. In react-hooks, drop two\nnon-load-bearing deviations and keep two load-bearing ones with\nfile:line-cited comments (prefer-for-of off for useClickOutside.js;\nthe test-file override for useCopyToClipboard.test.js/useId.test.js).\n\nAlso clean up the loop''s state file: mark U20 done, and remove stale\nduplicate entries in ## Next (U3-U15/U12-PR block and the U14\nsub-unit-E list) that were already completed under different unit\nlabels with matching commits.\n\n* chore(loop): archive migrate-styled-system-to-tonic-ui (Phase 2 complete)\n\nHeader + ## Done + full ## Log copied to .states/_archive/ so the\ncompleted loop stays visible/minable after .states/<name>/ is\nremoved. Phase 3/4 (provisional, gated on PR #1168 merging to main)\nnever started under this loop and are intentionally not archived\nhere per protocol — flagged in the archive''s closing note.\n\n* chore(loop): extract Phase 3/4 provisional plan before dir removal\n\nFull context (open questions, resolutions, provisional V1-V7/W1-Wfinal\nunit lists) for the parked v4-theme-token phases, preserved outside\nthe loop directory being deleted next.\n\n* chore(loop): remove migrate-styled-system-to-tonic-ui loop directory\n\nPhase 2 is complete (archived in .states/_archive/); Phase 3/4\nprovisional plan preserved there too. Final act of the completion\nprotocol.\n\n* fix(loop): archive the full final STATE.md, not extracted sections\n\nPer loop-engineering v1.2, the archive should preserve the whole\noriginal final state file, not just header+Done+Log. Replaces the\nextracted archive with the exact STATE.md content from immediately\nbefore the loop directory was removed.\n\n* fix(loop): restore the loop''s docs/ into the archive too\n\nThe docs/ directory (token-mapping.md, port-plan.md, jsdoc-dts-plan.md,\nversion-config-plan.md) was deleted along with STATE.md but never\narchived, leaving the archived STATE.md''s own ## Docs section\npointing at nothing. Restored all 4 files byte-for-byte from history.\n\n* chore(loop): trim archived docs to the one with forward-looking value\n\nDrop port-plan.md, jsdoc-dts-plan.md, version-config-plan.md from the\narchive -- execution plans for now-fully-shipped Phase 2 units with no\nforward dependency (the archived STATE.md''s Done/Log already records\nwhat happened, with commit refs). Move token-mapping.md -- the one\ndoc Phase 3 (v4 semantic tokens) will actually need -- to the repo''s\ntop-level docs/plans/ instead of nesting it under the loop archive,\nand repoint the archived STATE.md''s ## Docs entry accordingly.\n\n* chore(loop): drop ## Docs entry for token-mapping.md\n\nA new skill will own token mapping going forward, so the archived\nloop''s state no longer needs to reference it. The doc itself stays\nat docs/plans/2026-06-26-token-mapping.md for that skill to build on.\n\n* chore(loop): drop archived note and redundant phase3-4 extract\n\nThe full STATE.md already carries Phase 3/4''s provisional plan in\n## Next, making the standalone phase3-4-provisional-plan.md\nredundant. The archived note was bookkeeping about the archival\nprocess itself, not loop content worth keeping.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWv8YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtm0QAKFdqFw6bcQMMHWlJU44PI8i\nH7Muz48Z+30NW/XKrpWCZhFd4HPpCZb+030qam2mn1PT9+omdLRUW4bzi0KGV51X\nTGsM5Zve4S4pGhY9n6/rHVtTejNeKr2DUrwu0GhAV9OB7SaKGy4d4NPiNob6cRQ/\nDIze3dVJua2le00OfE7Q/i145CcuvF0VojhW/Zp