}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/c8dc661334826b91ebce98762719b1e320374128","node_id":"C_kwDODfyux9oAKGM4ZGM2NjEzMzQ4MjZiOTFlYmNlOTg3NjI3MTliMWUzMjAzNzQxMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/4603073d685d6bf791c314dfb3b3d38de5eb9315","sha":"4603073d685d6bf791c314dfb3b3d38de5eb9315","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/4603073d685d6bf791c314dfb3b3d38de5eb9315"}],"sha":"c8dc661334826b91ebce98762719b1e320374128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/c8dc661334826b91ebce98762719b1e320374128"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/447801?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/4603073d685d6bf791c314dfb3b3d38de5eb9315/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T06:06:43Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T06:06:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(react/portal): `Portal` now supports Shadow DOM by resolving its default container from the mounted root instead of `document.body`. (#1166)\n\n* fix(react/portal): resolve default portal container via getRootNode()\n\nPortal now resolves its default container from the root node of the tree it\nis mounted in, so portal-based components render inside a shadow root\nautomatically. Falls back to doc.body for iframe / normal page / detached\nfragments. An explicit containerRef still overrides.\n\n* docs(react-docs): sync environment + shadow-dom docs to latest, drop redundant color-mode/color-style pages\n\nSync the environment usage docs (iframe, shadow DOM, useEnvironment) and the\nshadow-dom customization page to their latest tonic-one content (createShadowDOM\npattern, useLayoutUnmount). Color mode / color style getting-started pages become\nsidebar redirects to their component pages.\n\n* chore(changeset): add changeset for Portal getRootNode (#1166)\n\n* fix(react-docs): redirect color-mode/color-style sidebar entries to component pages\n\nThe getting-started color-mode/color-style pages were removed; point their\nsidebar entries at the component pages with a LinkIcon redirect indicator so the\nnav no longer links to deleted pages.\n\n* docs(react-docs): reorganize sidebar with Environment and Icons entries\n\nAdd Environment and Icons component links, drop the MCP \"NEW\" tag,\nand move the AI assistant with MCP entry down the getting-started list.\n\n* feat: update llms.txt\n\n* docs(react-docs): remove micro-frontend link from environment See also\n\n* feat: enhance Portal to support Shadow DOM container\n\nThe `Portal` component now supports Shadow DOM by resolving its default container from the mounted root node instead of always using `document.body`. This change affects components like `Modal`, `Drawer`, `Popper`, `PortalManager`, and `ToastManager`, while maintaining existing iframe and normal-page behavior.\n\n* Update Portal feature description for Shadow DOM support","tree":{"sha":"89a6405efcf5ae3b368a8ff4a904332401cb3862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/89a6405efcf5ae3b368a8ff4a904332401cb3862"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/4603073d685d6bf791c314dfb3b3d38de5eb9315","verification":{"payload":"tree 89a6405efcf5ae3b368a8ff4a904332401cb3862\nparent e40a370806b4ea2208cba4c6c3c92e1b35216f68\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1782540403 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782540403 +0800\n\nfeat(react/portal): `Portal` now supports Shadow DOM by resolving its default container from the mounted root instead of `document.body`. (#1166)\n\n* fix(react/portal): resolve default portal container via getRootNode()\n\nPortal now resolves its default container from the root node of the tree it\nis mounted in, so portal-based components render inside a shadow root\nautomatically. Falls back to doc.body for iframe / normal page / detached\nfragments. An explicit containerRef still overrides.\n\n* docs(react-docs): sync environment + shadow-dom docs to latest, drop redundant color-mode/color-style pages\n\nSync the environment usage docs (iframe, shadow DOM, useEnvironment) and the\nshadow-dom customization page to their latest tonic-one content (createShadowDOM\npattern, useLayoutUnmount). Color mode / color style getting-started pages become\nsidebar redirects to their component pages.\n\n* chore(changeset): add changeset for Portal getRootNode (#1166)\n\n* fix(react-docs): redirect color-mode/color-style sidebar entries to component pages\n\nThe getting-started color-mode/color-style pages were removed; point their\nsidebar entries at the component pages with a LinkIcon redirect indicator so the\nnav no longer links to deleted pages.\n\n* docs(react-docs): reorganize sidebar with Environment and Icons entries\n\nAdd Environment and Icons component links, drop the MCP \"NEW\" tag,\nand move the AI assistant with MCP entry down the getting-started list.\n\n* feat: update llms.txt\n\n* docs(react-docs): remove micro-frontend link from environment See also\n\n* feat: enhance Portal to support Shadow DOM container\n\nThe `Portal` component now supports Shadow DOM by resolving its default container from the mounted root node instead of always using `document.body`. This change affects components like `Modal`, `Drawer`, `Popper`, `PortalManager`, and `ToastManager`, while maintaining existing iframe and normal-page behavior.\n\n* Update Portal feature description for Shadow DOM support","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqP2hzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApM8QAB3wSHe1xxq5G50dekkdqzY4\nfOtDYAft7al+epEVb5ItKQWtdeSzHaNkSJ3Z0+Ayj+zxlePw9zODuEGGQExksG6m\neor4s6ePacuM3LXwV+Orq5n/ZduuiDjOzz9/9FGHJqrMonJsdBAI5RdW5zsqYaRO\nhpAn/Ud90UY0OhNB7VYu5hWdyObBtfrk+/JLlaCRC9QISie0a6rp5LRBtQxiITk/\nPvWmOOZCUBBivBMYclq71aQhxhvNdRcFP84fyZoO/xiqS/KFIBkDyK+hHiQIavj+\nMpSBCCT3HgtRSsVoJldCjf+ePQtQybqhxA+olJP0+Zly2E3v/QfCeOWXmVdr/fCV\n1AZDORgsNCH33MeAA+weenoXcVEvVGFqwqqdjlehI9S0GiXxz7MMzaT4HR8mojZ/\n4OGWHvR/X7+KlUZrkz80g4rL35DGbslEC4UmN4lGiGo2x/H5c4vgMC44c9sHBMjE\nNYkY/xrVug0ly5UfaFClTknwNIXbqMCa6WLWdc2GPP7jqfB1aUprrGrtZkVkwOGx\nHloz616wO363c9mSP8w+yQhf0