/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/795e1061a5901eea5a3e6d5eb91f16a57a375839/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-09T08:11:11Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-09T08:11:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: upgrade eslint-config-trendmicro and fix lint errors (#1140)\n\n* ci(release): migrate npm publishing to OIDC Trusted Publishing\n\n* chore(deps-dev): upgrade eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.0 and align eslint versions\n\n* docs(babel): document @babel/preset-react runtime and importSource options\n\n* chore(eslint): fix __fixtures__ ignore pattern to match nested paths\n\n* fix(mcp): attach caught error as cause and remove stale eslint-disable comments\n\n* chore(react): remove unused React imports and fix lint errors\n\n* chore(react-base): remove unused React import from Box.test.js\n\n* chore(react-hooks): remove unused React imports and fix lint errors\n\n* fix(react-hooks): replace placeholder with aria-label in useEventCallback test\n\n* chore(react-icons): remove unused React imports from icon files\n\n* chore(utils): remove stale eslint-disable comments\n\n* chore(react-docs): adopt eslint-config-trendmicro and dedupe import plugin\n\nExtend the shared eslint-config-trendmicro base and strip the duplicate\n`import` plugin from next/core-web-vitals compat output to prevent\n\"Cannot redefine plugin\" errors.\n\n* chore(scripts): clean up build scripts and config\n\n- react-icons/build-icons.mjs: remove React import from generated\n  icon component templates\n- react-docs/update-style-props.mjs: use isNullish from @tonic-ui/utils\n- react-docs/next.config.mjs: use single quotes for consistency\n\n* chore(deps): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.1\n\nUpdate eslint-config-trendmicro across all packages from ^4.1.0 to ^4.1.1.\n\n* chore(deps): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.2\n\nUpdate eslint-config-trendmicro across all packages from ^4.1.1 to ^4.1.2.\n\n* chore(deps): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.3\n\nUpdate eslint-config-trendmicro across all packages from ^4.1.2 to ^4.1.3.\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix eslint errors across docs pages and components\n\n- Apply eslint --fix autofixes across demo pages and components\n- Fix consistent-return in TableOfContents useEffect early return\n- Return no-op cleanup in scrollable tabs and shadow-dom useEffects\n- Replace == with === in creating-tags keyCode check\n- Disable jsx-a11y/anchor-is-valid and no-alert in react-docs config\n  for intentional demo patterns\n- Disable tabindex-no-positive for ButtonBox positive tabIndex test\n\n* chore(react): fix lint warnings and bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.5\n\n- css-baseline/base-css.js: use dot notation for font theme keys\n- drawer/styles.js, modal/styles.js: suppress dot-notation on theme token keys\n- highlight/utils.js: suppress no-useless-escape on regex special chars\n- toast/ToastManager.js: remove stale eslint-disable-line no-useless-assignment\n- toast/__tests__/ToastManager.test.js: extract UpdatedToastContent component\n  outside TestComponent to avoid react/no-unstable-nested-components warning\n- utils/__tests__/isValidComponent.test.js: suppress react/prefer-stateless-function\n  on intentional class component used for test coverage\n- utils/descendant/useDescendant.js: replace useState with useReducer for force-update\n- eslint.config.mjs: remove redundant rule overrides now covered by eslint-config-trendmicro\n- Bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.5 across all packages\n\n* test(react): add tests to improve coverage for CSSBaseline, Descendant, Menu, TonicProvider, and isValidComponent\n\n* fix(react): remove spurious async from Menu test to satisfy require-await\n\n* chore(react-docs): remove unused React imports and bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.2.0\n\nStrip `React` from imports in ~500 docs files now that the new JSX\ntransform no longer requires it. Bump eslint-config-trendmicro to\n^4.2.0 across packages to pick up the rule change that surfaces these\nas errors.\n\n* chore: fix eslint errors in mcp and utils packages\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix eslint errors across docs pages and components\n\n* chore(react-docs): refine eslint config rules and add trendmicro preset\n\nDisable rules that conflict with documentation demo patterns (placeholder\nlinks, alerts, console usage, inline handlers) and add a max-len warning\nwith generous limits for doc code samples.\n\n* chore(react): clean up lint-related code in LinkButton test and resize-handle utils\n\n* chore(deps): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.3.0\n\nRemove the @stylistic/max-len override in react-docs eslint config now that the upstream preset provides an appropriate default.\n\n* chore(eslint): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.4.1 and fix resulting warnings\n\n- Bump eslint-config-trendmicro across all packages from ^4.3.0 to ^4.4.1.\n- prefer-const: change let to const where never reassigned; remove\n  shadowing declaration in InputControl so cleanup disconnects the\n  MutationObserver as intended.\n- Remove unused // eslint-disable-line no-unused-vars directives on\n  catch clauses.\n- react/hook-use-state: rename setters to match set<Value> pattern;\n  replace force-rerender useState with useReducer; drop useState for\n  values that never change.\n- react/no-unstable-nested-components: hoist NavList/NavItem and\n  InnerComponent out of parent components; suppress inline where the\n  wrapper is memoized and passed as a slot prop.\n- react/no-danger: suppress inline in _document with context comments\n  for the analytics loader and pre-paint color-mode script.\n- jsx-a11y/control-has-associated-label: add aria-label to bare\n  range inputs and the gomoku canvas; add text children to datalist\n  options.\n\n* chore(codecov): make patch informational and tighten project gate\n\nFlip patch check to informational so cleanup PRs with tiny diffs\n(e.g., 2/4 lines = 50%) no longer block merges against the auto\ntarget. Tighten project threshold from 2% to 1% and add\nremoved_code_behavior: adjust_base to neutralize deletion noise,\nkeeping project as the real regression gate. Also add if_ci_failed\nand if_not_found guardrails.\n\n* fix(react): use index as key in FormErrorMessage list to avoid React node collisions\n\nErrors may be passed as React nodes (e.g., JSX elements), which collide as\n`[object Object]` keys and trigger duplicate-key warnings. Switch back to\nindex-based keys with an inline eslint-disable for `react/no-array-index-key`.\n\n* chore(react-docs): add missing semicolon in CodeBlock import\n\n* refactor(react): rename map parameter to `error` in FormErrorMessage list\n\n* refactor(react): memoize getIsPassiveListenerSupported via IIFE\n\nConvert the closure factory into an IIFE so the memoization state is\ncaptured once at module load instead of per call. Also add a TODO to\nabstract the global `window` reference behind an environment provider.\n\n* chore: remove unused React import\n\n* chore: migrate react-docs Highlight usage and modernize utils test isolation\n\n- Replace `react-highlight-words` with the built-in `Highlight` component from\n  `@tonic-ui/react` in InstantSearchRefinementList and SearchDropdownFilterTag,\n  dropping the now-unused custom highlight styles and `useColorStyle` hook.\n- Switch the resize-handle utils test to `jest.isolateModulesAsync` with\n  dynamic `import()` so module isolation works with ESM.\n\n* refactor(react-docs): extract dropdown menu list style and tidy DropdownBase\n\nMove the menu list sizing logic out of DropdownBase into a dedicated\n`getMenuListStyle` helper in `experiments/dropdown/styles.js`, supporting\n`portalled`, `fit-toggle`, and default sizing modes with a shared 40vh\nmax height. In DropdownBase, drop the unused `useTheme` dependency,\nnormalize `renderItemProp` via `ensureFunction`, and convert the\nrecursive `renderItems` to a memoized `useCallback` with an inner helper\nto thread the key prefix.","tree":{"sha":"0b72ae731be3a91fade57309c955d0ac91d4810b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/0b72ae731be3a91fade57309c955d0ac91d4810b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/795e1061a5901eea5a3e6d5eb91f16a57a375839","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b72ae731be3a91fade57309c955d0ac91d4810b\nparent 2f1383cd1a00cfec8879c7b8bce30d022578b12c\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1778314271 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778314271 +0800\n\nchore: upgrade eslint-config-trendmicro and fix lint errors (#1140)\n\n* ci(release): migrate npm publishing to OIDC Trusted Publishing\n\n* chore(deps-dev): upgrade eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.0 and align eslint versions\n\n* docs(babel): document @babel/preset-react runtime and importSource options\n\n* chore(eslint): fix __fixtures__ ignore pattern to match nested paths\n\n* fix(mcp): attach caught error as cause and remove stale eslint-disable comments\n\n* chore(react): remove unused React imports and fix lint errors\n\n* chore(react-base): remove unused React import from Box.test.js\n\n* chore(react-hooks): remove unused React imports and fix lint errors\n\n* fix(react-hooks): replace placeholder with aria-label in useEventCallback test\n\n* chore(react-icons): remove unused React imports from icon files\n\n* chore(utils): remove stale eslint-disable comments\n\n* chore(react-docs): adopt eslint-config-trendmicro and dedupe import plugin\n\nExtend the shared eslint-config-trendmicro base and strip the duplicate\n`import` plugin from next/core-web-vitals compat output to prevent\n\"Cannot redefine plugin\" errors.\n\n* chore(scripts): clean up build scripts and config\n\n- react-icons/build-icons.mjs: remove React import from generated\n  icon component templates\n- react-docs/update-style-props.mjs: use isNullish from @tonic-ui/utils\n- react-docs/next.config.mjs: use single quotes for consistency\n\n* chore(deps): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.1\n\nUpdate eslint-config-trendmicro across all packages from ^4.1.0 to ^4.1.1.\n\n* chore(deps): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.2\n\nUpdate eslint-config-trendmicro across all packages from ^4.1.1 to ^4.1.2.\n\n* chore(deps): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.3\n\nUpdate eslint-config-trendmicro across all packages from ^4.1.2 to ^4.1.3.\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix eslint errors across docs pages and components\n\n- Apply eslint --fix autofixes across demo pages and components\n- Fix consistent-return in TableOfContents useEffect early return\n- Return no-op cleanup in scrollable tabs and shadow-dom useEffects\n- Replace == with === in creating-tags keyCode check\n- Disable jsx-a11y/anchor-is-valid and no-alert in react-docs config\n  for intentional demo patterns\n- Disable tabindex-no-positive for ButtonBox positive tabIndex test\n\n* chore(react): fix lint warnings and bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.5\n\n- css-baseline/base-css.js: use dot notation for font theme keys\n- drawer/styles.js, modal/styles.js: suppress dot-notation on theme token keys\n- highlight/utils.js: suppress no-useless-escape on regex special chars\n- toast/ToastManager.js: remove stale eslint-disable-line no-useless-assignment\n- toast/__tests__/ToastManager.test.js: extract UpdatedToastContent component\n  outside TestComponent to avoid react/no-unstable-nested-components warning\n- utils/__tests__/isValidComponent.test.js: suppress react/prefer-stateless-function\n  on intentional class component used for test coverage\n- utils/descendant/useDescendant.js: replace useState with useReducer for force-update\n- eslint.config.mjs: remove redundant rule overrides now covered by eslint-config-trendmicro\n- Bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.1.5 across all packages\n\n* test(react): add tests to improve coverage for CSSBaseline, Descendant, Menu, TonicProvider, and isValidComponent\n\n* fix(react): remove spurious async from Menu test to satisfy require-await\n\n* chore(react-docs): remove unused React imports and bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.2.0\n\nStrip `React` from imports in ~500 docs files now that the new JSX\ntransform no longer requires it. Bump eslint-config-trendmicro to\n^4.2.0 across packages to pick up the rule change that surfaces these\nas errors.\n\n* chore: fix eslint errors in mcp and utils packages\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix eslint errors across docs pages and components\n\n* chore(react-docs): refine eslint config rules and add trendmicro preset\n\nDisable rules that conflict with documentation demo patterns (placeholder\nlinks, alerts, console usage, inline handlers) and add a max-len warning\nwith generous limits for doc code samples.\n\n* chore(react): clean up lint-related code in LinkButton test and resize-handle utils\n\n* chore(deps): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.3.0\n\nRemove the @stylistic/max-len override in react-docs eslint config now that the upstream preset provides an appropriate default.\n\n* chore(eslint): bump eslint-config-trendmicro to ^4.4.1 and fix resulting warnings\n\n- Bump eslint-config-trendmicro across all packages from ^4.3.0 to ^4.4.1.\n- prefer-const: change let to const where never reassigned; remove\n  shadowing declaration in InputControl so cleanup disconnects the\n  MutationObserver as intended.\n- Remove unused // eslint-disable-line no-unused-vars directives on\n  catch clauses.\n- react/hook-use-state: rename setters to match set<Value> pattern;\n  replace force-rerender useState with useReducer; drop useState for\n  values that never change.\n- react/no-unstable-nested-components: hoist NavList/NavItem and\n  InnerComponent out of parent components; suppress inline where the\n  wrapper is memoized and passed as a slot prop.\n- react/no-danger: suppress inline in _document with context comments\n  for the analytics loader and pre-paint color-mode script.\n- jsx-a11y/control-has-associated-label: add aria-label to bare\n  range inputs and the gomoku canvas; add text children to datalist\n  options.\n\n* chore(codecov): make patch informational and tighten project gate\n\nFlip patch check to informational so cleanup PRs with tiny diffs\n(e.g., 2/4 lines = 50%) no longer block merges against the auto\ntarget. Tighten project threshold from 2% to 1% and add\nremoved_code_behavior: adjust_base to neutralize deletion noise,\nkeeping project as the real regression gate. Also add if_ci_failed\nand if_not_found guardrails.\n\n* fix(react): use index as key in FormErrorMessage list to avoid React node collisions\n\nErrors may be passed as React nodes (e.g., JSX elements), which collide as\n`[object Object]` keys and trigger duplicate-key warnings. Switch back to\nindex-based keys with an inline eslint-disable for `react/no-array-index-key`.\n\n* chore(react-docs): add missing semicolon in CodeBlock import\n\n* refactor(react): rename map parameter to `error` in FormErrorMessage list\n\n* refactor(react): memoize getIsPassiveListenerSupported via IIFE\n\nConvert the closure factory into an IIFE so the memoization state is\ncaptured once at module load instead of per call. Also add a TODO to\nabstract the global `window` reference behind an environment provider.\n\n* chore: remove unused React import\n\n* chore: migrate react-docs Highlight usage and modernize utils test isolation\n\n- Replace `react-highlight-words` with the built-in `Highlight` component from\n  `@tonic-ui/react` in InstantSearchRefinementList and SearchDropdownFilterTag,\n  dropping the now-unused custom highlight styles and `useColorStyle` hook.\n- Switch the resize-handle utils test to `jest.isolateModulesAsync` with\n  dynamic `import()` so module isolation works with ESM.\n\n* refactor(react-docs): extract dropdown menu list style and tidy DropdownBase\n\nMove the menu list sizing logic out of DropdownBase into a dedicated\n`getMenuListStyle` helper in `experiments/dropdown/styles.js`, supporting\n`portalled`, `fit-toggle`, and default sizing modes with a shared 40vh\nmax height. In DropdownBase, drop the unused `useTheme` dependency,\nnormalize `renderItemProp` via `ensureFunction`, and convert the\nrecursive `renderItems` to a memoized `useCallback` with an inner helper\nto thread the key prefix.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/uwfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOKIQAFAxGXX6hdpRdu4PCfyNfp3h\nd5pNLjniINhaptcKmMilmEYL96iK8wTAoG/pvGIC7UzPmbC0VmUrwefuiHJ+T0ff\nimy1f8NNZd4Q0XpSFStbhnY+htl31MRAFPI/EzKv9Se1ZWvEbH3p5Y5TGUWntpSX\nAZy6X322zxqB59OwFH9NLkmJyQjfA8TQaNXvACWEInJjiANjWKhzbr+/heJ7C53V\nA52jXJyQuWbtp2idFa/8tyJ+yHXEUTIPCHqVjsRoAuTbEhJnDtzYu9QBei7epFna\no0FRW5FkxLzn5rD+ZDPTNkNLVCe5P+/1botyti2vTmgaBp4cEWVKAQoFXy4GHROa\njEvou/iubfUVRUy1GrTOvAotdn8JNvMQ4aP/x82CIbLam04mq2laR/ld6BzEz1XZ\nbgTd80jLUkhy7iguYvaPKzPupj+7IsG3q+oYsujeh7hLWSYV6eystbDox9nXTS8R\nxJdomH63u+lM5D6idy321dFLjX5a0ZEiT3fKg4JKgYCTjh3yepYYdeD157QWzRz2\nluVf6j83qna2KMHT0+jh33hsNjMc6w0gOxoh5kQCUTIkbCW6AAxwI6nJKk/O4Ivs\n/yV7qruKFF3YgcuMOoW9PG/HsG5iqWAecZHPepRNENVQ6ajtC92PL5U7me4uOraY\n7D+wGAdDcXLIvZIHTucq\n=dBmh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-09T