d_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/272eb84827049f9c266e903635ea6016c2a5f533","node_id":"C_kwDODfyux9oAKDI3MmViODQ4MjcwNDlmOWMyNjZlOTAzNjM1ZWE2MDE2YzJhNWY1MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/0a66cfbcba753d127927bebe5f349863b2251c08","sha":"0a66cfbcba753d127927bebe5f349863b2251c08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/0a66cfbcba753d127927bebe5f349863b2251c08"}],"sha":"272eb84827049f9c266e903635ea6016c2a5f533","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/272eb84827049f9c266e903635ea6016c2a5f533"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/447801?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cheton","id":447801,"login":"cheton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzgwMQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commits/0a66cfbcba753d127927bebe5f349863b2251c08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-09T16:23:31Z","email":"447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cheton Wu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-09T16:23:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: migrate ESLint from v8 eslintrc to v9 flat config (#1110)\n\n* chore: migrate ESLint from v8 eslintrc to v9 flat config\n\n- Replace all .eslintrc.js files with eslint.config.js using ESLint v9\n  flat config format across all packages\n- Upgrade eslint-config-trendmicro from ^3.0.0 to ^4.0.0, which ships\n  a native flat config array (no FlatCompat needed)\n- Upgrade eslint-config-next from 14.x to 16.1.6 for react-docs, which\n  also supports native flat config via eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals\n- Remove FlatCompat and its path/url boilerplate from all configs\n- Remove redundant eslint-plugin-react-hooks imports from react, react-base,\n  react-hooks, react-icons — now bundled inside eslint-config-trendmicro v4\n\n* chore(eslint): migrate to flat config (ESLint 9)\n\n- Rename eslint.config.js -> eslint.config.mjs in all packages\n- Remove .eslintignore files; migrate to ignores in eslint.config.mjs\n- Remove @babel/eslint-plugin (incompatible with flat config, unused)\n- Upgrade globals to v15 (fixes AudioWorkletGlobalScope whitespace issue)\n- Upgrade eslint-plugin-react to v7.37.5 (ESLint 9 support)\n- Upgrade eslint-plugin-import to v2.32.0 (ESLint 9 support)\n- Upgrade eslint-plugin-react-hooks to v7.0.1 (ESLint 9 support)\n- Upgrade eslint-config-next to v15 in react-docs\n- Use FlatCompat for eslint-config-next (legacy config bridge)\n- Fix @typescript-eslint flat config: use flat/recommended and flat/stylistic\n- Fix no-unused-vars in catch blocks across source files\n- Fix eqeqeq violations in sx.js and highlight/utils.js\n\nWIP: some react-hooks/react-compiler rules are still failing\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix ESLint errors from React Compiler rules\n\nResolves build failures in @tonic-ui/react-docs caused by stricter\nrules introduced in eslint-plugin-react-hooks v5+ (React Compiler).\n\nChanges by category:\n\n- Add `/* eslint-disable react-hooks/set-state-in-effect */` to docs\n  example files that intentionally call setState in effects (async\n  data loading, controlled component sync, game state, etc.)\n\n- Add `/* eslint-disable react-hooks/refs */` to docs example files\n  that intentionally access refs during render (useEventCallback\n  comparison, useConst demo, scrollbar FAQ)\n\n- Add `/* eslint-disable react-hooks/purity */` to useConst demo\n  that calls Math.random() as an intentional example\n\n- Add `/* eslint-disable no-constant-binary-expression */` to the\n  sx-prop array-of-objects example using `true && {}`\n\n- Add `// eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/incompatible-library`\n  before each useReactTable() call (TanStack Table returns unstable\n  function references incompatible with React Compiler memoization)\n\n- Fix useOnce/useOnceWhen examples to use useState instead of reading\n  ref.current during render\n\n- Fix unused catch bindings using optional catch binding syntax\n\n- Remove unused eslint-disable directives in ColorStyleBlock and\n  TableOfContents components\n\n- Upgrade @tanstack/react-table from ^8.9.1 to ^8.21.3\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix remaining ESLint errors and clean up unused code\n\n- Remove unused `colorKey` prop from ColorStyleBlock and its call site in ColorStyleBody\n- Remove stale eslint-disable comment in TableOfContents (exhaustive-deps no longer needed)\n- Refactor useCallback/useEventCallback demo files to track onChange invalidations\n  using useLayoutEffect + useState(-1) instead of refs accessed during render,\n  fixing react-hooks/refs violations without storing the callback reference in state\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix react-hooks/refs errors without eslint-disable comments\n\n- faq-scroll-position: replace useRef with useState for scroll position\n  so scrollTop is read from state rather than a ref during render\n- reordering-rows-with-react-dnd: move drag(drop(ref)) into useEffect\n  to avoid passing a ref to a function during render\n- scrollable: replace useMemo with useEffect+useRef for the debounced\n  scroll handler to avoid creating a ref-reading closure during render\n- AutosizeInput: rewrite using callEventHandlers, rename to onChange,\n  and use useCallback to defer ref access outside of render\n\n* chore(deps): pin eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y to ^6.10.2 across all packages\n\nReplace `latest` tag with explicit `^6.10.2` version to ensure consistent\ndependency resolution and avoid pulling in outdated 6.8.0 builds.\n\n* chore(eslint): standardize globals and languageOptions across all packages\n\n- Replace globalThis: ''readonly'' and versioned globals with ...globals.es2025\n  (cumulative superset of all earlier es20xx presets, includes globalThis,\n  BigInt, AggregateError, WeakRef, FinalizationRegistry, Iterator, etc.)\n- Order globals es2025 → browser → node → jest (most universal first)\n- Add sourceType: ''module'' explicitly to all packages so configs remain\n  correct if trendmicroConfig is removed in the future\n- Remove ecmaVersion: 2020 from mcp (ignored by @typescript-eslint/parser)\n- Remove ecmaVersion: ''latest'' from react-docs (flat config default)\n- Replace globals.es2015 in react-docs with globals.es2025 (superset)\n- Fix json-stringify.js: use catch (_error) over optional catch binding\n\n* test(styled-system): add coverage for null and undefined in responsive arrays\n\nExercises both branches of the `=== null || === undefined` check in\n`createResponsiveResolver` to bring patch coverage to 100%.\n\n* chore(deps): move globals from root to each package devDependencies\n\nConsistent with how eslint and jest are declared per-package rather than\nat the workspace root.\n\n* chore: update yarn.lock","tree":{"sha":"dbfdb95a2aacac8e1c39fa2873fc6deeb0571ab2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/trees/dbfdb95a2aacac8e1c39fa2873fc6deeb0571ab2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/git/commits/0a66cfbcba753d127927bebe5f349863b2251c08","verification":{"payload":"tree dbfdb95a2aacac8e1c39fa2873fc6deeb0571ab2\nparent 1dad579923e09d6356bd84ab4a90023df85f9e09\nauthor Cheton Wu <447801+cheton@users.noreply.github.com> 1775751811 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775751811 +0800\n\nchore: migrate ESLint from v8 eslintrc to v9 flat config (#1110)\n\n* chore: migrate ESLint from v8 eslintrc to v9 flat config\n\n- Replace all .eslintrc.js files with eslint.config.js using ESLint v9\n  flat config format across all packages\n- Upgrade eslint-config-trendmicro from ^3.0.0 to ^4.0.0, which ships\n  a native flat config array (no FlatCompat needed)\n- Upgrade eslint-config-next from 14.x to 16.1.6 for react-docs, which\n  also supports native flat config via eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals\n- Remove FlatCompat and its path/url boilerplate from all configs\n- Remove redundant eslint-plugin-react-hooks imports from react, react-base,\n  react-hooks, react-icons — now bundled inside eslint-config-trendmicro v4\n\n* chore(eslint): migrate to flat config (ESLint 9)\n\n- Rename eslint.config.js -> eslint.config.mjs in all packages\n- Remove .eslintignore files; migrate to ignores in eslint.config.mjs\n- Remove @babel/eslint-plugin (incompatible with flat config, unused)\n- Upgrade globals to v15 (fixes AudioWorkletGlobalScope whitespace issue)\n- Upgrade eslint-plugin-react to v7.37.5 (ESLint 9 support)\n- Upgrade eslint-plugin-import to v2.32.0 (ESLint 9 support)\n- Upgrade eslint-plugin-react-hooks to v7.0.1 (ESLint 9 support)\n- Upgrade eslint-config-next to v15 in react-docs\n- Use FlatCompat for eslint-config-next (legacy config bridge)\n- Fix @typescript-eslint flat config: use flat/recommended and flat/stylistic\n- Fix no-unused-vars in catch blocks across source files\n- Fix eqeqeq violations in sx.js and highlight/utils.js\n\nWIP: some react-hooks/react-compiler rules are still failing\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix ESLint errors from React Compiler rules\n\nResolves build failures in @tonic-ui/react-docs caused by stricter\nrules introduced in eslint-plugin-react-hooks v5+ (React Compiler).\n\nChanges by category:\n\n- Add `/* eslint-disable react-hooks/set-state-in-effect */` to docs\n  example files that intentionally call setState in effects (async\n  data loading, controlled component sync, game state, etc.)\n\n- Add `/* eslint-disable react-hooks/refs */` to docs example files\n  that intentionally access refs during render (useEventCallback\n  comparison, useConst demo, scrollbar FAQ)\n\n- Add `/* eslint-disable react-hooks/purity */` to useConst demo\n  that calls Math.random() as an intentional example\n\n- Add `/* eslint-disable no-constant-binary-expression */` to the\n  sx-prop array-of-objects example using `true && {}`\n\n- Add `// eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/incompatible-library`\n  before each useReactTable() call (TanStack Table returns unstable\n  function references incompatible with React Compiler memoization)\n\n- Fix useOnce/useOnceWhen examples to use useState instead of reading\n  ref.current during render\n\n- Fix unused catch bindings using optional catch binding syntax\n\n- Remove unused eslint-disable directives in ColorStyleBlock and\n  TableOfContents components\n\n- Upgrade @tanstack/react-table from ^8.9.1 to ^8.21.3\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix remaining ESLint errors and clean up unused code\n\n- Remove unused `colorKey` prop from ColorStyleBlock and its call site in ColorStyleBody\n- Remove stale eslint-disable comment in TableOfContents (exhaustive-deps no longer needed)\n- Refactor useCallback/useEventCallback demo files to track onChange invalidations\n  using useLayoutEffect + useState(-1) instead of refs accessed during render,\n  fixing react-hooks/refs violations without storing the callback reference in state\n\n* chore(react-docs): fix react-hooks/refs errors without eslint-disable comments\n\n- faq-scroll-position: replace useRef with useState for scroll position\n  so scrollTop is read from state rather than a ref during render\n- reordering-rows-with-react-dnd: move drag(drop(ref)) into useEffect\n  to avoid passing a ref to a function during render\n- scrollable: replace useMemo with useEffect+useRef for the debounced\n  scroll handler to avoid creating a ref-reading closure during render\n- AutosizeInput: rewrite using callEventHandlers, rename to onChange,\n  and use useCallback to defer ref access outside of render\n\n* chore(deps): pin eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y to ^6.10.2 across all packages\n\nReplace `latest` tag with explicit `^6.10.2` version to ensure consistent\ndependency resolution and avoid pulling in outdated 6.8.0 builds.\n\n* chore(eslint): standardize globals and languageOptions across all packages\n\n- Replace globalThis: ''readonly'' and versioned globals with ...globals.es2025\n  (cumulative superset of all earlier es20xx presets, includes globalThis,\n  BigInt, AggregateError, WeakRef, FinalizationRegistry, Iterator, etc.)\n- Order globals es2025 → browser → node → jest (most universal first)\n- Add sourceType: ''module'' explicitly to all packages so configs remain\n  correct if trendmicroConfig is removed in the future\n- Remove ecmaVersion: 2020 from mcp (ignored by @typescript-eslint/parser)\n- Remove ecmaVersion: ''latest'' from react-docs (flat config default)\n- Replace globals.es2015 in react-docs with globals.es2025 (superset)\n- Fix json-stringify.js: use catch (_error) over optional catch binding\n\n* test(styled-system): add coverage for null and undefined in responsive arrays\n\nExercises both branches of the `=== null || === undefined` check in\n`createResponsiveResolver` to bring patch coverage to 100%.\n\n* chore(deps): move globals from root to each package devDependencies\n\nConsistent with how eslint and jest are declared per-package rather than\nat the workspace root.\n\n* chore: update yarn.lock","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp19KECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfRgQAAiwWQZJhuQwoai5PX6LQpvh\nqHbt31Aqt23vvo2ujN/rm1g7uflTO+0+fBbVydQSviAvpvv+OJDCcGM0n4Ki8rJL\nhUS068lUU5aN6WNdkaZTOxMDfeNoznFRF8INb+PDwy/jus/IJiZXlqVzHzGQWSJW\noMygoCOjtX+eG86Evw2HpkJhbCoiWBrxi9punO0FeiGiXm6L8Kp6wd81VEmnvans\n0HF6KIAS/joBnUMO0PTi+cqXwoU++lrl/idfFyDWeZla6A5XgJk9/soBCrEU23i3\no7hpjOmZt+dh168Pr2lc7a1ZVktQ1X1y/EvBu4Lz8npNB9cgZWbqlZyvkG3mVnXk\nsNpc1z7Nc3nxjyaEq8OW+MAaSyf+3sflCovxJqSi/j0ezsSmh3NIpPi1m5i0Z9Rr\nq4CeB2BYBWlArgigKC6DQWfJF7H8rJ4ExRKSoJ3Uif59wpCrp8LcZGg0nAhd1jb0\nHwPyz8SDzfgVX9XDwPJ1waVrZDfyu19jOyacFdhcdyECxhypPt7jJ32k/gV/v5uB\nxVdVwaVJzIFsKdZye0uiRcXIiUmqb/Gw7dPoDkNJyf+aBTTc7c0JHlYCMtU80Sfq\nzwBGI+UMvkxwQOAb02UogOxevH/tjxX3WZPXG3sCmX195/OU+JUXmrSYFlCN4fWp\nfa1tLvIsM1FHC1F+il0X\n=EJom\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-09T16:23:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trendmicro-frontend/tonic-ui/commit/0a66cfbcba753d127927bebe5f349863b2251c08","node_id